(window.LINGUA_BOOK=window.LINGUA_BOOK||{}).condense=Object.assign(window.LINGUA_BOOK.condense||{},{"part-013-chapter-13-psycholinguistics-and-neurolinguistics":{"title":{"en":"[In progress] Chapter 13: Psycholinguistics and Neurolinguistics","zh":"第 13 章：心理语言学与神经语言学"},"summary":{"en":"This chapter explores experiments in psycholinguistics and neurolinguistics that reveal how language works in the human mind, and shows how experimental evidence can support the concepts of linguistic theory introduced in earlier chapters. Readers will learn about key experimental methods, how to back theoretical claims with experimental evidence, and why linguistics is viewed as part of cognitive science.","zh":"本章探讨心理语言学与神经语言学的实验，揭示语言在人脑中的运作方式，并说明实验证据如何支持前几章提出的语言学理论概念。读者将了解若干重要的实验方法，学会用实验证据支撑理论主张，并理解语言学为何被视为认知科学的一部分。"},"points":[{"en":"Experiments in psycholinguistics and neurolinguistics reveal how language works in the human mind.","zh":"心理语言学与神经语言学的实验揭示语言在人类心智中的运作方式。"},{"en":"Experimental evidence can be used to support concepts from linguistic theory.","zh":"实验证据可以用来支持语言学理论中的概念。"},{"en":"The chapter introduces important experimental methods and explains why linguistics belongs to cognitive science.","zh":"本章介绍重要的实验方法，并解释语言学为何属于认知科学。"}],"terms":[{"en":"psycholinguistics","zh":"心理语言学","defEn":"interdisciplinary field that tests hypotheses about linguistic representations and processes in the mind","defZh":"通过实验检验关于心智中语言表征与语言加工过程之假设的交叉学科"},{"en":"neurolinguistics","zh":"神经语言学","defEn":"research area studying how language is organized and implemented in the biology of the brain","defZh":"研究语言如何在人脑的生物学基础上组织与实现的研究领域"},{"en":"cognitive science","zh":"认知科学","defEn":"broader field of research into the mind, of which linguistics forms one part","defZh":"研究心智的更大研究领域，语言学是其中的一个组成部分"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"This chapter turns to experiments in psycholinguistics and neurolinguistics, the two research areas that investigate how language is realized in the human mind and brain. The aim is to show how findings from controlled experiments can serve as evidence for the concepts of linguistic theory developed in earlier chapters, and to introduce some of the methods that produce that evidence.","zh":"本章转向心理语言学与神经语言学的实验，这两个研究领域考察语言如何在人的心智与大脑中实现。目的是说明受控实验的发现如何为前几章建立的语言学理论概念提供证据，并介绍产生这些证据的若干方法。"},{"en":"By the end of the chapter, readers should be able to describe several important experimental methods in these fields, use experimental evidence to support claims made in theoretical linguistics, and explain why linguistics is regarded as part of cognitive science.","zh":"学完本章，读者应能描述这两个领域中若干重要的实验方法，用实验证据支持理论语言学提出的主张，并解释语言学为何被视为认知科学的一部分。"}]},"chapter-147-the-mind-makes-language":{"title":{"en":"13.1 The mind makes language","zh":"13.1 心智创造语言"},"summary":{"en":"Linguistic hypotheses about phonemes, morphemes and phrase structure are really hypotheses about how the mind represents language. Psycholinguists test such claims with behavioural experiments, while neurolinguists study how the language system is implemented in the brain, using methods from cognitive neuroscience and data from language disorders.","zh":"关于音位、语素、短语结构等语言学假设，实际上都是关于心智如何表征语言的假设。心理语言学家用行为实验检验这类主张，神经语言学家则借助认知神经科学的方法以及语言障碍的数据，研究语言系统如何在大脑中实现。"},"points":[{"en":"Linguistic hypotheses about phonemes, morphemes and phrase structure are hypotheses about mental representation.","zh":"关于音位、语素、短语结构的语言学假设，其实是关于心智表征的假设。"},{"en":"A classical view of cognitive science gives the mind symbolic representations plus operations that transform them.","zh":"认知科学的经典观点认为心智拥有符号表征，以及对这些表征进行转换的操作。"},{"en":"Mental grammars are the means by which linguistic representations are transformed, for example before speech.","zh":"心智语法是转换语言表征的手段，例如在说出话语之前进行的转换。"},{"en":"Psycholinguists devise behavioural experiments, such as measuring how quickly a word decision is made.","zh":"心理语言学家设计行为实验，例如测量对单词做出判断的速度。"},{"en":"Neurolinguists study how the cognitive system of language is organized in the brain's biology.","zh":"神经语言学家研究语言这一认知系统如何在大脑的生物学基础上组织起来。"}],"terms":[{"en":"cognitive science","zh":"认知科学","defEn":"field that studies the mind and its symbolic representations and operations","defZh":"研究心智及其符号表征与操作的研究领域"},{"en":"symbolic representation","zh":"符号表征","defEn":"mental symbol standing for something, transformed by mental operations","defZh":"心智中代表某事物的符号，可被心智操作所转换"},{"en":"mental grammar","zh":"心智语法","defEn":"the means by which linguistic representations are transformed in the mind","defZh":"心智中用以转换语言表征的机制"},{"en":"psycholinguistics","zh":"心理语言学","defEn":"interdisciplinary field devising experiments on linguistic representations and processes in the mind","defZh":"设计实验研究心智中语言表征与加工过程的交叉学科"},{"en":"neurolinguistics","zh":"神经语言学","defEn":"research focusing on how language is organized and implemented in the brain","defZh":"着重研究语言如何在大脑中组织与实现的研究"}],"examples":[{"text":"measuring how quickly someone can make a decision about a word after seeing it on a computer screen","noteEn":"A behavioural method used by psycholinguists to probe mental processing.","noteZh":"心理语言学家用来探究心智加工过程的一种行为方法。"},{"text":"a phoneme is encoded into the appropriate phone according to the phonological rules of the language prior to being spoken","noteEn":"Illustrates mental grammars transforming linguistic representations before speech.","noteZh":"说明心智语法在说话之前对语言表征进行转换。"},{"text":"examining disorders of language that arise from problems in the brain, for example following a stroke or other brain injury","noteEn":"Data source for neurolinguists alongside cognitive neuroscience methods.","noteZh":"神经语言学家除认知神经科学方法之外的数据来源。"}],"body":[{"en":"Linguistics belongs to cognitive science. The hypotheses developed in this book about phonemes, morphemes and phrase structure are, in a real sense, hypotheses about how the human mind represents language. On the classical view, the mind contains symbolic representations together with operations that transform them; within that framework, mental grammars are the machinery by which linguistic representations are changed. In spoken languages, for instance, a phoneme is converted into the appropriate phone by the phonological rules of the language before it is spoken.","zh":"语言学属于认知科学。本书关于音位、语素、短语结构等提出的假设，实际上都是关于人类心智如何表征语言的假设。按照经典观点，心智包含符号表征以及转换这些表征的操作；在这一框架内，心智语法就是改变语言表征的机制。例如在有声语言中，音位在说出之前会依据该语言的音系规则转换为相应的音素。"},{"en":"Native speakers' intuitions sometimes provide enough evidence that a particular element or rule forms part of the mind's capacity for language, but linguists often want other kinds of evidence, or want to know how those elements are deployed in production and comprehension. Psycholinguistics is the interdisciplinary field in which researchers design experiments to test hypotheses about linguistic representations and processes in the mind, normally using behavioural methods.","zh":"母语者的直觉有时足以证明某一语言要素或规则是心智语言能力的一部分，但语言学家往往需要其他类型的证据，或者想了解这些要素在语言产出与理解中如何被调用。心理语言学正是这样一个交叉学科领域：研究者设计实验，检验关于心智中语言表征与加工过程的假设，通常采用行为方法。"},{"en":"Psycholinguists also propose and evaluate theories of mental processes, while this chapter stresses the link between their findings and linguistic theory. Underlying both fields is the assumption that the mind has a biological basis in the brain. Neurolinguists ask how language as a cognitive system is organized and implemented biologically, drawing on cognitive neuroscience methods and on language disorders that follow stroke or other brain injury. They too may evaluate linguistic theory while pursuing theories of their own.","zh":"心理语言学家还提出并评估关于心智过程的理论，而本章着重强调其研究发现与语言学理论之间的联系。两个领域都以下述假设为基础：心智在大脑中有其生物学基础。神经语言学家追问语言这一认知系统如何在生物学上组织与实现，所依据的是认知神经科学的方法，以及中风或其他脑损伤之后出现的语言障碍。他们同样既评估语言学理论，也发展自己的理论。"},{"en":"Because both fields are far too vast to summarize in a single chapter, the chapter concentrates on experiments that give further evidence for important concepts from earlier chapters, and highlights some of the key experimental methods these researchers use.","zh":"由于这两个领域都过于庞大，无法在一章之内予以概括，本章集中介绍那些为前几章重要概念提供进一步证据的实验，并着重说明研究者使用的一些关键实验方法。"}]},"chapter-148-evidence-for-phonemes-as-mental-categories":{"title":{"en":"13.2 Evidence for phonemes as mental categories","zh":"13.2 音位作为心理范畴的证据"},"summary":{"en":"Every language organizes speech sounds into its own phonological system, which forms part of a speaker's mental grammar. Thinking of a phoneme as a mental category predicts that the brain should treat acoustically different sounds as the same. Using MEG, Phillips and colleagues (2000) found a phonological Mismatch Negativity, showing that the brain accesses phonological categories early in auditory processing.","zh":"每种语言都把语音组织成自己的音系系统，该系统构成说话人心智语法的一部分。把音位看作心理范畴，可以预测大脑会把声学上不同的语音当作同一类。Phillips 等人（2000）用脑磁图发现了一种音系层面的失匹配负波，表明大脑在听觉加工的早期就已通达音位范畴。"},"points":[{"en":"Two sounds that are allophones of one phoneme in a language may be separate phonemes in another.","zh":"在一门语言中属于同一音位的两个音位变体，在另一门语言中可能是不同的音位。"},{"en":"Each language has its own phonological system, which is part of the speaker's mental grammar.","zh":"每种语言都有自己的音系系统，它是说话人心智语法的一部分。"},{"en":"A phoneme can be viewed as a mental category of speech sounds that the mind maps sounds onto.","zh":"音位可以视为语音的心理范畴，心智把听到的语音归入其中。"},{"en":"The Mismatch Negativity is a brain response to a stimulus that stands out from repeated background stimuli.","zh":"失匹配负波是大脑对与重复背景刺激不同的刺激所做出的反应。"},{"en":"Phillips et al. (2000) used a voicing contrast whose many-to-one relation existed only at the phonological level.","zh":"Phillips 等人（2000）使用的浊音对立，其多对一关系只存在于音系层面。"},{"en":"The phonological mismatch effect arose in auditory cortex, early in perceptual processing.","zh":"音系层面的失匹配效应出现在听觉皮层，即知觉加工的早期阶段。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phoneme","zh":"音位","defEn":"smallest unit in a language that can create contrast between words","defZh":"一种语言中能够造成词与词之间对立的最小单位"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"one of the variant speech sounds that realize a single phoneme","defZh":"实现同一个音位的若干变异语音之一"},{"en":"minimal pair","zh":"最小对立对","defEn":"two words differing in meaning and in only one phoneme","defZh":"意义不同而仅相差一个音位的两个词"},{"en":"Voice Onset Time","zh":"浊音起始时间","defEn":"time between release of a stop and the beginning of vowel voicing","defZh":"塞音除阻到元音开始振动之间的时间"},{"en":"Mismatch Negativity","zh":"失匹配负波","defEn":"negative-going brain response to a stimulus that mismatches repeated stimuli","defZh":"与重复刺激不匹配的刺激所引发的负向脑电反应"},{"en":"magnetoencephalography (MEG)","zh":"脑磁图","defEn":"method recording magnetic field changes, locating brain responses better than EEG","defZh":"记录磁场变化的方法，定位脑反应来源优于脑电图"}],"examples":[{"text":"The English words pat (/pæt/) and bat (/bæt/) differ only in the initial phoneme (/p/ or /b/), but have different meanings.","noteEn":"A minimal pair showing that /p/ and /b/ are separate English phonemes.","noteZh":"一个最小对立对，说明 /p/ 与 /b/ 是英语中彼此对立的音位。"},{"text":"[pʰ] vs. [p]","noteEn":"Aspirated and unaspirated stops that cannot contrast in English.","noteZh":"送气与不送气的塞音，在英语中不能构成对立。"},{"text":"speakers of English perceive a /t/ sound when Voice Onset time is above about 25ms, and a /d/ sound when it is below","noteEn":"The sharp perceptual boundary between the /d/ and /t/ categories.","noteZh":"/d/ 与 /t/ 两个范畴之间界限分明的知觉边界。"},{"text":"many other languages that treat [pʰ] and [p] as separate phonemes, for example Hindi and Thai","noteEn":"Languages whose phonology categorizes the same sounds differently.","noteZh":"音系把同样两个语音归为不同音位的语言。"}],"body":[{"en":"Chapter 4 showed that every language has its own phonology: two sounds that are allophones of one phoneme in one language may be separate phonemes in another. Each language thus organizes speech sounds into a phonological system that belongs to speakers' mental grammar. This section reviews experiments supporting the idea that phonology is something the mind and brain actually do.","zh":"第 4 章指出，每种语言都有自己的音系：在一门语言中属于同一音位的两个音位变体，在另一门语言中可能是彼此对立的音位。因此每种语言都把语音组织成属于自己的音系系统，该系统属于说话人心智语法的一部分。本节考察支持下述看法的实验：音系确实是心智与大脑所做的事情。"},{"en":"A phoneme is the smallest unit that can create contrast, so exchanging one phoneme for another can create a minimal pair. English pat (/pæt/) and bat (/bæt/) differ only in the initial phoneme yet mean different things, showing that /p/ and /b/ are separate phonemes. A phoneme can also be called a mental category of speech sounds. English voiceless stops like /p/ are aspirated ([pʰ]) at the start of a stressed syllable, but [pʰ] and [p] cannot contrast in English because they are variants of one phoneme, so the mind maps both onto /p/. Hindi and Thai, by contrast, treat them as separate phonemes.","zh":"音位是能够造成对立的最小单位，用一个音位替换另一个音位可以构成最小对立对。英语的 pat（/pæt/）与 bat（/bæt/）只在首音位上不同，意义却不同，说明 /p/ 与 /b/ 是英语中彼此对立的音位。音位也可以说是语音的心理范畴。英语中 /p/ 这类清塞音在重读音节开头会送气（[pʰ]），但 [pʰ] 与 [p] 在英语中不能构成对立，因为它们只是同一个音位的变体，心智把二者都归入 /p/。相比之下，印地语和泰语把它们视为不同的音位。"},{"en":"Phonological analysis reveals a speaker's categories, but here the question is whether the brain itself maps acoustically varying sounds onto one category. Phillips and colleagues (2000) sought a surprise response to a sound in a different phonological category. Earlier research had established the Mismatch Negativity, a reaction to a rare tone differing in frequency from repeated tones, measurable even when listeners ignore the sounds.","zh":"音系分析借助最小对立对或语音出现环境的描写来揭示说话人的范畴，但本节的问题是：大脑本身是否会把声学上有差异的语音归入同一范畴。Phillips 等人（2000）寻找大脑对属于不同音系范畴的语音产生的惊奇反应。此前的研究已确立失匹配负波：当少数音调的频率不同于重复出现的音调时，大脑会产生这种反应，即使听者不注意声音也能测到。"},{"en":"Using magnetoencephalography (MEG), which records magnetic field changes and locates their source better than EEG, Phillips et al. tested the voicing contrast between /dæ/ and /tæ/, which differ in Voice Onset Time. English speakers hear /t/ when VOT is above about 25ms and /d/ when it is below, a sharp switch, yet VOT varies within each category. The many-to-one relation thus existed only phonologically, not acoustically, and it elicited a phonological Mismatch Negativity originating in an auditory part of the brain, showing that phonological contrasts are accessed early in perceptual processing.","zh":"Phillips 等人使用脑磁图（MEG），它记录磁场变化，定位反应来源优于脑电图（EEG），考察了 /dæ/ 与 /tæ/ 之间的浊音对立，二者之别在于浊音起始时间。英语使用者听到浊音起始时间高于约 25 毫秒的音时判定为 /t/，低于该值时判定为 /d/，转换是突变而非渐变的，但在每个范畴内部浊音起始时间仍有差异。因此多对一关系只存在于音系层面而非纯声学层面，它引发了音系层面的失匹配负波；该反应源自大脑处理听觉信息的部分，说明音系对立在知觉加工的早期就被通达。"}]},"chapter-149-in-progress-evidence-for-language-specific-phonology":{"title":{"en":"13.3 Evidence for language-specific phonology","zh":"13.3 语言特定音系学的证据"},"summary":{"en":"Evidence from behavioural and electrophysiological studies shows that speakers hear speech through the phonology of their native language. English and Bengali both nasalize vowels, but only Bengali makes nasality phonemic, so Bengali listeners reach a word's recognition point later than English listeners. Japanese and French listeners likewise differ on illegal codas.","zh":"来自行为实验与电生理实验的证据表明，母语音系左右着人们听辨语音的方式。英语和孟加拉语都会使元音鼻化，但只有孟加拉语把鼻化对立当作音位区别，因此孟加拉语听者到达词语识别点的时间晚于英语听者。日本语与法语听者在处理非法韵尾时也表现出差异。"},"points":[{"en":"English nasal vowels are allophones of one phoneme; Bengali has a nasal/oral minimal pair.","zh":"英语的鼻化元音是同一音位的变体；孟加拉语则存在鼻化/口元音的最小对立对。"},{"en":"English listeners identify ban or bad before the final consonant, using vowel nasality predictively.","zh":"英语听者在听到末尾辅音之前就能分辨 ban 与 bad，依靠元音鼻化作出预测。"},{"en":"Bengali listeners need more input before recognising a word with a nasal vowel.","zh":"孟加拉语听者需要更多输入才能识别含鼻化元音的词语。"},{"en":"Japanese phonotactics ban oral codas, so listeners mentally insert a vowel into igmo.","zh":"日本语的音位配列禁止口辅音作韵尾，听者会在心里给 igmo 增补一个元音。"},{"en":"The Mismatch Negativity response reflected French but not Japanese speakers' sensitivity to the /u/.","zh":"失匹配负波的脑反应显示只有法语听者察觉 /u/ 的有无，日本语听者则不然。"}],"terms":[{"en":"nasalization","zh":"鼻化","defEn":"A process making a vowel nasal under the influence of a neighbouring nasal consonant.","defZh":"在相邻鼻辅音的影响下，使元音带上鼻音成分的音系过程。"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"A predictable variant of a phoneme, such as nasalized and oral [æ] in English.","defZh":"某个音位可预测的变体形式，如英语中鼻化与口元音版本的 [æ]。"},{"en":"minimal pair","zh":"最小对立对","defEn":"Two words differing in one sound that nevertheless carry different meanings.","defZh":"只在一个语音上不同、但意义不同的两个词，用于证明该音位地位。"},{"en":"phonotactics","zh":"音位配列（语音组合法）","defEn":"Language-specific restrictions on which sounds may combine in a syllable.","defZh":"某一语言对音节内音素组合方式的限制规则，如禁止某类韵尾。"},{"en":"epenthesis","zh":"增音","defEn":"Insertion of a sound, here a vowel that repairs an illegal syllable coda.","defZh":"插入一个音（此处为元音）以修补不合法的音节韵尾。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[bæ̃n]","noteEn":"English ban, where the vowel is nasal because of the following /n/.","noteZh":"英语 ban 的发音，元音因后面的 /n/ 而鼻化。"},{"text":"/bãd/ (which means ‘dam’) and /bad/ (which means ‘difference’)","noteEn":"The Bengali minimal pair showing that nasality is phonemic.","noteZh":"孟加拉语最小对立对，说明鼻化在该语言中具有音位地位。"},{"text":"/ɹipoʊɹt/","noteEn":"report, used to illustrate how an onset cohort shrinks as more sounds arrive.","noteZh":"report，用来演示音节首候选集如何随语音输入增加而缩小。"},{"text":"igumo and igmo","noteEn":"Fake words contrasting legal and illegal codas in Japanese phonotactics.","noteZh":"两个假词，对比日本语音位配列中合法与不合法的韵尾。"}],"body":[{"en":"Both English and Bengali nasalize vowels before nasal consonants, yet the status of that nasality differs sharply. In English the oral and nasal versions of a vowel never distinguish words, so they count as allophones of a single phoneme. Bengali instead pairs /bãd/ ‘dam’ with /bad/ ‘difference’, a minimal pair proving that /a/ and /ã/ are separate phonemes stored in the mental grammar.","zh":"英语和孟加拉语都会在鼻辅音前使元音鼻化，但鼻化在两种语言中的地位截然不同。在英语中，元音的口音与鼻音版本从不对立成词，因此它们只是同一个音位的音位变体。孟加拉语则把表示‘堤坝’的 /bãd/ 与表示‘差别’的 /bad/ 配成最小对立对，证明 /a/ 与 /ã/ 是心理语法中彼此独立的音位。"},{"en":"Marslen-Wilson and Lahiri tested whether this phonological difference shapes spoken word recognition. Because words unfold over time, listeners activate an onset cohort and eliminate candidates as evidence accumulates, until they reach the word's recognition point. Using a gating task, in which progressively longer fragments are played for identification, they found that English listeners could decide between ban and bad before the final consonant arrived, exploiting the vowel's nasality to anticipate it. Bengali listeners, for whom a nasal vowel may precede either a nasal or an oral consonant, required more of the signal and reached a later recognition point.","zh":"Marslen-Wilson 与 Lahiri 检验了这一音系差异是否会影响口语词汇识别。由于词语随时间展开，听者会激活一个音节首候选集，并随证据增加排除候选，直至到达该词的识别点。他们采用门控任务，把录音切成越来越长的片段让被试辨认，结果发现英语听者在末尾辅音出现之前就能在 ban 与 bad 之间作出判断，利用元音鼻化来预判后接辅音；而孟加拉语听者面对既可接鼻辅音又可接口辅音的鼻化元音，需要更多信号，识别点因而更晚。"},{"en":"A second line of evidence comes from event-related potentials. Dehaene-Lambertz and colleagues presented French and Japanese listeners with fake words such as igumo and igmo. Since /gm/ cannot begin a syllable, igmo would have to be syllabified ig.mo, which French allows but Japanese forbids because oral consonants cannot be codas. When a sequence changed only by the presence or absence of /u/, French listeners judged the final item different and produced a Mismatch Negativity; Japanese listeners largely judged the items the same and showed no such response. The likely explanation is that Japanese listeners mentally repaired the illegal form by inserting a vowel, effectively hearing igumo. Native phonology thus shapes perception itself.","zh":"第二类证据来自事件相关电位。Dehaene-Lambertz 等人让法语与日本语听者听 igumo、igmo 这样的假词。由于 /gm/ 无法充当音节首，igmo 只能切分为 ig.mo，这在法语中允许，在日本语中却因口辅音不能作韵尾而被禁止。当序列仅在 /u/ 的有无上发生变化时，法语听者判断最后一个词不同，并产生失匹配负波；日本语听者大多认为两者相同，也没有出现该反应。最可能的解释是，日本语听者在心里通过增音修补了非法形式，实际上听到的是 igumo。可见母语音系直接影响知觉本身。"}]},"chapter-150-slug-13-4-evidence-for-top-down-effects-of-word-knowledge-on-perception":{"title":{"en":"13.4 Evidence for ‘top-down’ effects of word knowledge on perception","zh":"13.4 词语知识对知觉的‘自上而下’效应的证据"},"summary":{"en":"Categorical perception makes listeners hearing a continuum of Voice Onset Time report either [d] or [t] with a sharp boundary, yet the effect is not phonological knowledge, since infants and chinchillas show it too. Ganong showed that word knowledge biases the judgement: ambiguous stops are heard as the sound that yields a real English word. Such top-down effects show knowledge shaping early perceptual processing.","zh":"范畴感知使听者在聆听连续的嗓音起始时间时，会在一个清晰边界两侧分别报告 [d] 或 [t]，但该效应并不源于音系知识，因为婴儿和毛丝鼠也表现出同样现象。Ganong 证明词语知识会偏斜判断：歧义的塞音被听成能够构成真实英语单词的那个音。这类自上而下效应表明知识会影响早期的知觉加工。"},"points":[{"en":"Voice Onset Time varies continuously, but listeners hear a sharp [d]/[t] boundary.","zh":"嗓音起始时间是连续变化的，但听者感知到的是 [d] 与 [t] 之间的清晰边界。"},{"en":"Categorical perception also occurs for non-native contrasts, infants, and non-human animals.","zh":"范畴感知也出现在非母语对立、婴儿以及非人类动物身上。"},{"en":"Ganong found ambiguous sounds are more often labelled as the member of a real word.","zh":"Ganong 发现歧义音更容易被归入那个能构成真实单词的类别。"},{"en":"The Ganong effect demonstrates that word knowledge biases which speech sound is heard.","zh":"Ganong 效应表明词语知识会左右人们实际听到的是哪个语音。"},{"en":"Bottom-up information comes from sensory surfaces; top-down influences come from knowledge.","zh":"自下而上的信息来自感觉表面；自上而下的影响则来自听者的知识。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Voice Onset Time","zh":"嗓音起始时间","defEn":"The interval between the release of a stop closure and the start of voicing.","defZh":"塞音除阻时刻与后续元音声带振动开始之间的时间间隔。"},{"en":"categorical perception","zh":"范畴感知","defEn":"Hearing a continuous acoustic continuum as discrete categories with a sharp boundary.","defZh":"把连续变化的声学连续统听成边界清晰的离散范畴的现象。"},{"en":"bottom-up information","zh":"自下而上的信息","defEn":"Information entering the brain from sensory surfaces such as the inner ear or retina.","defZh":"经由内耳、视网膜等感觉表面进入大脑的外部信息。"},{"en":"top-down influence","zh":"自上而下的影响","defEn":"An effect of the listener's knowledge, such as word knowledge, on perceptual processing.","defZh":"听者已有知识（如词语知识）对知觉加工过程产生的效应。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[d]","noteEn":"The voiced stop at the low end of the continuum.","noteZh":"连续统低端的有声塞音。"},{"text":"[t]","noteEn":"The voiceless stop at the high end of the continuum.","noteZh":"连续统高端的清塞音。"},{"text":"dash","noteEn":"A real English word chosen for one end of the continuum.","noteZh":"连续统一端所选的真实英语单词。"},{"text":"tash","noteEn":"A pronounceable but non-existent English word at the other end.","noteZh":"另一端可发音但并非真实英语单词的形式。"}],"body":[{"en":"Earlier sections showed that phonological knowledge shapes speech perception. Word knowledge does the same. A useful starting point is categorical perception. The voiced stop [d] and the voiceless stop [t] differ in Voice Onset Time, the lag between the release of the stop closure and the onset of the following vowel. Although this variable is continuous and can take any millisecond value, listeners who hear a series of tokens report one category below a boundary and the other above it, with only a narrow band of uncertainty in between.","zh":"前文表明音系知识会塑造语音知觉，词语知识同样如此。可以从范畴感知谈起：有声塞音 [d] 与清塞音 [t] 的差别在于嗓音起始时间，即塞音除阻与后续元音开始之间的时间差。尽管这一变量是连续的、可以取任意毫秒值，听者在听一系列刺激时却会在某个边界以下报告同一范畴、在边界以上报告另一范畴，中间只有一条狭窄的不确定地带。"},{"en":"Categorical perception was once taken as evidence for phonology, but that view met counterevidence. The same sharp boundary appears for contrasts absent from a listener's language, for babies whose mental grammars are not yet tuned, and even for non-human animals such as chinchillas, which presumably lack human phonology. Hence the square brackets for [d] and [t] here: the contrast is phonetic rather than phonemic.","zh":"范畴感知一度被视为音系知识的证据，但这一解释遇到了反证。同样的清晰边界也出现在听者母语中并不存在的对立上，出现在心理语法尚未定型的婴儿身上，甚至出现在毛丝鼠等大概不具备人类音系能力的非人类动物身上。因此本节对 [d] 与 [t] 使用方括号：这里的对立属于语音层面而非音位层面。"},{"en":"Ganong built on these robust findings by embedding the continuum in words. One end of a continuum formed a real English word such as dash, while the other formed a pronounceable non-word such as tash. Listeners were more likely to label a sound near the threshold as the stop that made a genuine word: they heard dash rather than tash, and task rather than dask. This is the Ganong effect. Sensory input arriving from the ears is bottom-up information, and knowledge acting upon it, as word knowledge does here, is a top-down influence. The chapter's examples all show language knowledge at work very early in perception.","zh":"Ganong 在这些稳固发现的基础上，把连续统嵌入单词之中。连续统的一端构成 dash 这样的真实英语单词，另一端构成 tash 这样可发音但并非单词的形式。结果，听者更倾向于把接近阈值的音归为那个能造出真实单词的塞音：他们听到的是 dash 而非 tash，是 task 而非 dask，这就是 Ganong 效应。来自耳朵的感觉输入是自下而上的信息，而像词语知识这样作用于其上的知识则属于自上而下的影响。本章各例都说明语言知识在知觉的极早阶段就已发挥作用。"}]},"part-014-chapter-14-historical-linguistics":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 14: Historical Linguistics","zh":"第 14 章 历史语言学"},"summary":{"en":"Languages change constantly, from one generation to the next and even within a single generation, and they can change in any area where they differ: phonology, morphology, syntax, and others. This chapter surveys the many ways languages change and explains how linguists make educated guesses about what earlier languages looked like.","zh":"语言在不断变化，既发生在代际之间，也发生在同一代人内部；语言可以在音系、形态、句法等任何彼此不同的层面发生变化。本章考察语言变化的各种方式，说明语言学家如何依据证据对语言早期的面貌作出有根据的推测，并列出学完本章后应达到的学习目标。"},"points":[{"en":"Languages change from one generation to the next and even within a single generation.","zh":"语言会一代代发生变化，甚至在同一代人的内部也会发生变化。"},{"en":"Change can occur in any domain where languages differ, including phonology, morphology, and syntax.","zh":"语言在音系、形态、句法等任何存在差异的层面都可能发生变化。"},{"en":"The chapter teaches readers to categorize changes, reconstruct proto-forms, and refute common myths.","zh":"本章教读者给变化归类、构拟原始形式，并反驳关于语言变化的常见误解。"},{"en":"Sections 14.1-14.6 and 14.8-14.9 are complete but are still subject to change.","zh":"14.1 至 14.6 节与 14.8 至 14.9 节已经完成，但仍然可能修改。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonology","zh":"音系学","defEn":"The study of how sounds pattern and function in a language.","defZh":"研究语音在语言中如何系统分布并发挥功能的语言学分支。"},{"en":"morphology","zh":"形态学","defEn":"The study of the internal structure and formation of words.","defZh":"研究词的内部结构、构成方式及其变化的语言学分支。"},{"en":"syntax","zh":"句法学","defEn":"The study of how words combine into phrases and sentences.","defZh":"研究词如何组合成短语和小句、句子的一门语言学分支。"},{"en":"proto-form","zh":"原始形式（构拟形式）","defEn":"A reconstructed ancestral form inferred from patterns in the available linguistic data.","defZh":"根据现有语言材料中的规律推断并构拟出来的共同祖语形式。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"Historical linguistics is the study of how languages change over time. Because languages can differ from one another in phonology, morphology, syntax, and other areas, they can also change in each of those areas, from one generation to the next and even within a single generation. This chapter surveys the many kinds of change that languages undergo and explains how linguists make reasoned guesses about earlier stages of a language.","zh":"历史语言学研究语言如何随时间发生变化。语言可以在音系、形态、句法等各个层面彼此不同，因此也可以在每一个层面发生变化，既可能发生在代际之间，也可能发生在同一代人内部。本章介绍语言所能经历的各种变化，并说明语言学家如何对语言的早期面貌作出有根据的推测。"},{"en":"By the end of the chapter readers should be able to label examples of change with the appropriate technical terms, analyze linguistic data to identify which changes are illustrated and to reconstruct proto-forms, and recognize and argue against widespread myths about language change. The chapter is still being written: Sections 14.1-14.6 and 14.8-14.9 are complete but may change, and further sections are planned, including 14.7 External change, 14.10 More comparative reconstruction, and 14.11 Language families.","zh":"学完本章后，读者应能：用专业术语给语言变化的实例归类；分析语言材料，判断其中体现了哪些变化并构拟原始形式；识别并反驳关于语言变化的常见误解。本章仍在编写中：14.1 至 14.6 节和 14.8 至 14.9 节已经完成但可能修改，后续还将增加 14.7 外部变化、14.10 更多比较构拟、14.11 语系等小节。"}]},"chapter-151-slug-14-1-why-do-languages-change":{"title":{"en":"14.1 Why do languages change?","zh":"14.1 语言为什么会变化？"},"summary":{"en":"Languages change because the world they describe changes and because speakers naturally vary. Change may come from outside the language, as in language contact, or from internal pressures such as ease of articulation, and it is not linked to complexity. Linguists study such change synchronically, at one point in time, or diachronically, across two or more points in time.","zh":"语言变化既因为它所描述的世界在变化，也因为说话者本身存在变异。变化可来自语言外部（如语言接触），也可来自发音省力等内部压力，并且与语言的复杂度无关。语言学家以共时视角研究某一时间点，以历时视角研究两个或多个时间点之间的变化。"},"points":[{"en":"New technology and cultural shifts push speakers to coin or adapt short terms for frequently discussed concepts.","zh":"新科技与文化变迁促使说话者为经常谈论的概念创造或改造简短词语。"},{"en":"Variation may be stable, but a variant can spread until older forms become obsolete and socially unremarkable.","zh":"变异可能长期稳定，但某一变式也可能扩散，使旧形式最终被淘汰、不再有社会含义。"},{"en":"Synchronic linguistics studies one point in time; diachronic linguistics studies change across two or more periods.","zh":"共时语言学研究某一时间点，历时语言学研究两个或多个时期之间的变化。"},{"en":"Labels such as Old, Middle, and Modern describe attested periods, and their boundaries are gradual and language-specific.","zh":"古、中古、现代等标签用于有据可考的时期，其界限渐变且因语言而异。"},{"en":"Change may come from external sources such as language contact or from internal pressures such as ease of articulation.","zh":"变化或源于语言接触等外部因素，或源于发音省力等语言内部压力。"},{"en":"Language change and complexity are unrelated, because complexity is not a single well-defined property.","zh":"语言变化与复杂度并无关联，因为复杂度并非单一而明确的属性。"}],"terms":[{"en":"synchronic linguistics","zh":"共时语言学","defEn":"The study of language patterns at a single point in time.","defZh":"研究语言在某一特定时间点上的模式与结构的语言学分支。"},{"en":"diachronic linguistics","zh":"历时语言学","defEn":"The study of changes in language patterns across two or more points in time.","defZh":"研究语言模式在两个或多个时间点之间发生变化的语言学分支。"},{"en":"etymology","zh":"词源","defEn":"The historical development of a word or expression.","defZh":"一个词或表达方式在历史上的来源、形成与意义演变过程。"},{"en":"etymological fallacy","zh":"词源谬误","defEn":"An argument relying on an older etymological meaning where only the current meaning matters.","defZh":"在只应依据当前意义时，却以词的古老词源意义进行论证的逻辑谬误。"},{"en":"external change","zh":"外部变化","defEn":"Language change caused by something outside the language, such as cultural change or language contact.","defZh":"由语言之外的因素引起的变化，如文化变迁、新科技或语言接触。"},{"en":"internal change","zh":"内部变化","defEn":"Language change that happens spontaneously within the language because of its structure or modality.","defZh":"因语言自身结构或模态而在语言内部自发产生、无需外部原因的变化。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the house is building > the house is being built","noteEn":"An older English construction was replaced by a newer passive progressive form.","noteZh":"英语中较旧的进行被动结构逐渐被较新的被动进行式取代。"},{"text":"reasons [rezənz] > [rizənz]","noteEn":"A vowel change that destroyed a pun in Shakespeare's Henry IV.","noteZh":"一次元音变化，使莎士比亚《亨利四世》中的双关语失效。"},{"text":"nice 'silly' > 'delicate' > 'careful' > 'pleasant'","noteEn":"The meaning of nice shifted repeatedly after it was borrowed into English.","noteZh":"nice 一词借入英语后，其词义经历了多次连续的演变。"},{"text":"If reasons were as plentiful as blackberries, […]","noteEn":"Falstaff's pun depended on the word reasons sounding like raisins.","noteZh":"福斯塔夫的这个双关依赖于 reasons 与 raisins 读音相近。"}],"body":[{"en":"Languages change because the world they describe changes: new technology and cultural shifts demand new ways of talking. A sentence about an app, a blog, and a life hack would have been hard to decode in the 1990s. Frequently discussed concepts attract short specialized terms, so speakers coin or adapt expressions instead of repeating cumbersome descriptions. Languages also vary naturally, and a meaningful variant may displace older forms: the house is being built replaced the house is building, despite prescriptivists who called it clumsy.","zh":"语言之所以变化，是因为它所描述的世界在变化：新科技与文化变迁都需要新的说法。今天一句涉及 app、blog 和 life hack 的话，在 20 世纪 90 年代几乎无法解读。由于经常谈论的概念容易获得简短而专门的词语，说话者会创造或改造表达方式，而不愿反复使用冗长的描述。语言本身也在自然地变异，一个带有社会含义的变式最终可能取代旧形式：the house is being built 取代了 the house is building，尽管当时的规范主义者曾指责它笨拙。"},{"en":"Synchronic linguistics studies patterns at a single point in time; diachronic linguistics studies change across two or more points. When changes accumulate, modifiers such as Old, Middle, and Modern label periods: Old English (AD 450-1150), Middle English (1150-1500), and Modern English (1500-present). Such labels apply only to attested forms, those with direct written or recorded evidence. The boundaries are conventional and never sharp, since every period contained variation by class, age, gender, and region, and the transition from one period to the next is gradual.","zh":"共时语言学研究某一时间点上的语言模式，历时语言学研究两个或多个时间点之间的变化。当变化积累到一定程度，可用 Old、Middle、Modern 等修饰语标示时期：古英语（公元 450—1150 年）、中古英语（1150—1500 年）和现代英语（1500 年至今）。这些标签只用于有直接书面或录音证据的、有据可考的形式。时期界限是约定的，从不截然分明，因为任何时期都存在因阶层、年龄、性别和地域而产生的变异，而从一个时期到下一个时期的过渡是渐进的。"},{"en":"A change can be written with a greater-than sign from the older form to the newer one, as in reasons [rezənz] > [rizənz]. The notation also tracks meaning: nice, borrowed from Old French meaning 'silly', shifted through 'delicate' and 'careful' to 'pleasant'. A word's history is its etymology, but its meaning depends on current use, not on its source. Insisting on an older sense where only the modern one matters is the etymological fallacy; the suffix -phobic generally marks aversion or intolerance.","zh":"变化可以用大于号表示，由旧形式指向新形式，如 reasons [rezənz] > [rizənz]。这一记号也能表示意义变化：nice 借自中古法语，原义为「silly」，后经「delicate」「careful」演变为「pleasant」。一个词的历史演变过程就是它的词源，但词义取决于当下的用法，而与来源无关。在只应依据现代意义时坚持词源意义，就是词源谬误；-phobic 这一后缀一般表示厌恶或不容忍。"},{"en":"Change has two broad sources. External change originates outside the language, especially in language contact, when speakers of different languages interact. Internal change arises from a language's own structure: adjacent phones are easier to pronounce when they take on properties from one another through assimilation. Many internal changes probably begin during acquisition, as children articulate slightly differently from their parents, unnoticed at first but pushed further in later generations. Change and complexity are unrelated, because complexity is not a single well-defined property.","zh":"变化有两大来源。外部变化源于语言之外，尤其是不同语言的使用者相互接触之时。内部变化源于语言自身的结构：相邻的音素如果互相吸收特征而发生同化，发音会更省力。许多内部变化可能始于语言习得，儿童与父母的发音略有不同，起初无人察觉，却可能被后代进一步推进。变化与复杂度之间并无关联，因为复杂度并非单一而明确的属性。"}]},"chapter-152-slug-14-2-lexical-change":{"title":{"en":"14.2 Lexical change","zh":"14.2 词汇变化"},"summary":{"en":"Some changes are sporadic, affecting only one or a few words, as when app was clipped from application. Lexical change mostly adds words: neologisms may come from root creation, proper names, brand names and genericization, compounding, clipping, blending, or acronyms and initialisms. Taboo avoidance can also create new words or add meanings to existing ones.","zh":"有些变化是零星的，只影响一个或少数几个词，如 app 由 application 截短而来。词汇变化主要表现为新词增加：新词可来自词根创制、专有名词、品牌名与商标通用化、复合、截短、混成，以及首字母缩略与字母词。忌讳回避也能创造新词，或为已有词增添新义。"},"points":[{"en":"Sporadic changes affect only one or a few words, as when app was clipped from application but not complication.","zh":"零星变化只影响一个或少数几个词，如 app 由 application 截短而来，而 complication 并未如此。"},{"en":"A neologism is a word created inside a language; root creation coins one without deriving it from existing words.","zh":"新词指在语言内部创造的词；词根创制不依据已有词而直接造词。"},{"en":"Many new words come from proper names, brand names, or genericization, in which a trademark becomes a general term.","zh":"许多新词来自专有名词、品牌名或商标通用化，即商标变成一般词语。"},{"en":"Compounding, clipping, and blending build new words from existing material in different ways.","zh":"复合、截短与混成以不同的方式利用语言中已有的材料来构造新词。"},{"en":"Acronyms derive from spelling rather than pronunciation and may be read as words or letter by letter.","zh":"首字母缩略词依据拼写而非读音构成，可整体拼读或逐字母读出。"},{"en":"Taboo avoidance can add meaning to an existing word or create a neologism such as dang for damn.","zh":"忌讳回避既可以给已有词增添新的意义，也可以创造新词，如用 dang 代替 damn。"}],"terms":[{"en":"neologism","zh":"新词","defEn":"A new word or expression created within a language.","defZh":"在某一语言内部新创造出来、此前并不存在的词或表达方式。"},{"en":"root creation","zh":"词根创制","defEn":"Coining a new word that is not derived from any existing word.","defZh":"不依据任何已有词，直接创造出一个全新词语的构词方式。"},{"en":"clipping","zh":"截短（截短法）","defEn":"Creating a new word by shortening a longer existing word.","defZh":"通过截去较长词语的一部分来创造新词的方法，又称压缩或截断。"},{"en":"blend","zh":"混成词","defEn":"A word made by combining pieces of two or more words.","defZh":"把两个或更多词的部分组合成一个新词，又称拼缀词或混合词。"},{"en":"acronym","zh":"首字母缩略词","defEn":"A word formed from pieces of the spelling of a phrase.","defZh":"由短语中各词拼写的一部分构成的词，可按单词或按字母读。"},{"en":"genericization","zh":"商标通用化","defEn":"When a brand name comes to refer to any similar product regardless of brand.","defZh":"商标名称变为泛指任何同类产品、不再区分品牌的语义变化。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the shortened form app for application in English","noteEn":"A clipping that did not extend to similar words such as complication.","noteZh":"这一截短并没有波及 complication 等结构相似的词，只影响了 app 一个词。"},{"text":"brunch is a blend of breakfast and lunch","noteEn":"The clipped pieces [br-] and [-ʌnt͡ʃ] join to form [brʌnt͡ʃ].","noteZh":"brunch 是把 breakfast 截取的部分 [br-] 与 lunch 截取的部分 [-ʌnt͡ʃ] 组合起来形成的新词 [brʌnt͡ʃ]。"},{"text":"scuba < self-contained underwater breathing apparatus","noteEn":"An acronym that is pronounced as an ordinary word, namely [skubə].","noteZh":"可以像普通单词一样读出的首字母缩略词，读作 [skubə]。"},{"text":"dang and gosh entered English, as they were coined as alternatives to damn and God","noteEn":"Taboo avoidance creating new words rather than reusing existing ones.","noteZh":"忌讳回避不借用已有词，而是创造新词替代禁忌词。"}],"body":[{"en":"Some internal changes are sporadic: they affect only one or a few words. English app was shortened from application, but complication and implication were not shortened to comp or imp. A notable sporadic change is the shift of some two-handed signs in American Sign Language, such as COW, to one-handed signs, while BOOK and HALLOWEEN kept both hands. Lexical change usually means adding words. A word created inside a language without direct outside influence is a neologism; the most basic type, root creation, is rare and often imitative, as with zap or googol.","zh":"有些内部变化是零星的，只影响一个或少数几个词。英语的 app 由 application 截短而来，但 complication、implication 并没有截短为 comp、imp。另一个零星变化的例子是美国手语中某些双手手势（如 COW）变为单手手势，而 BOOK、HALLOWEEN 仍保留双手。词汇变化通常指新词的增加。在语言内部、不受外部直接影响而创造的词叫新词，最基本的类型是词根创制，这类词相当少见，且常带模仿性质，如 zap 和 googol。"},{"en":"Most neologisms are derived from words already in the language. Proper names are a rich source: canary is named after the Canary Islands, whose Latin name Canariæ Insulæ means 'Islands of the Dogs', so the birds are indirectly named after dogs. Brand names also produce words. When a brand name comes to refer to any similar product regardless of brand, genericization has occurred, as with dry ice, dumpster, escalator, heroin, and zipper, and sometimes the trademark still legally exists.","zh":"大多数新词都由语言中已有的词派生而来。专有名词是丰富的来源：canary（金丝雀）得名于加那利群岛，而群岛的拉丁语名称 Canariæ Insulæ 意为「狗之岛」，因此这种鸟其实是间接以狗命名的。品牌名也能产生新词。当品牌名转而泛指任何同类产品而不分品牌时，就发生了商标通用化，如 dry ice、dumpster、escalator、heroin、zipper；有时商标在法律上仍然存在。"},{"en":"New words can also be built from existing material. A compound joins two or more words, often with a non-compositional meaning. Clipping shortens a longer word, as in exam < examination and burger < hamburger, and rarely takes material from the middle, as in flu < influenza. A blend combines pieces of two or more words into a new word sharing their pronunciation and meaning: brunch joins [br-] from breakfast with [-ʌnt͡ʃ] from lunch.","zh":"新词也可以用已有材料构造。复合词把两个或更多单词组合起来，其意义往往不能由组成部分直接推知。截短通过缩短较长的词造词，如 exam < examination、burger < hamburger，极少数情况下截取词的中部，如 flu < influenza。混成词把两个或更多词的部分拼合，新词在读音和意义上都与原词相关：brunch 由 breakfast 的 [br-] 与 lunch 的 [-ʌnt͡ʃ] 组合为 [brʌnt͡ʃ]。"},{"en":"Acronyms come from the spelling of a word or phrase. They may be read as ordinary words, like scuba < self-contained underwater breathing apparatus, pronounced [skubə], or letter by letter, in which case they are initialisms, like SO < significant other, pronounced [ɛs o]. Acronyms are relatively modern, and most claimed acronym etymologies before the mid-twentieth century are false. Taboo avoidance also creates neologisms such as dang for damn and gosh for God.","zh":"首字母缩略词依据词或短语的拼写而非读音构成，可以像普通词一样读出，如 scuba < self-contained underwater breathing apparatus 读作 [skubə]；也可以逐字母读出，这时称为字母词，如 SO < significant other 读作 [ɛs o]。缩略词是相对晚近的现象，20 世纪中叶以前关于某词源自缩略的说法几乎都是错误的。忌讳回避也会创造新词，如用 dang 代替 damn、用 gosh 代替 God。"}]},"chapter-153-slug-14-3-phonological-change":{"title":{"en":"14.3 Phonological change","zh":"14.3 音系变化"},"summary":{"en":"Historical phonology largely reuses the same processes found synchronically, but adds sporadic types such as metathesis, spelling pronunciation, hyperforeignism, dissimilation, and analogy. Regular sound changes instead apply uniformly in a consistent environment, whether conditioned or unconditioned, and may merge, split, or merely shift phonemes. The Great Vowel Shift, a chain of overlapping non-merging shifts, rearranged the English long vowels.","zh":"历时音系变化大多沿用共时可见的音系过程，但还包括换位、拼写读音、过度外来化、异化和类比等零星变化。规则音变则在特定环境中一致地作用于所有可能的词，并可分为有条件与无条件两类；其结果可能造成音位合并、音位分裂，或仅是音位转移。英语长元音的大元音移位即由多项重叠而不合并的变化构成。"},"points":[{"en":"Metathesis swaps the positions of sounds, as in the ASL signs DEAF1 and DEAF2 or English ask versus axian.","zh":"换位使语音位置互换，如美国手语 DEAF1 与 DEAF2，或英语 ask 与历史上的 axian。"},{"en":"Spelling pronunciation shifts a word toward its spelling, as when Arctic gained [k] after being respelled from Latin.","zh":"拼写读音让发音向拼写靠拢，如 Arctic 依拉丁拼写重新拼写后读作 [ɑrktɪk]。"},{"en":"Hyperforeignism applies stereotypes about foreign languages, as with Beijing [beʒɪŋ] and coup de grâce [ku də ɡrɑ].","zh":"过度外来化套用对外语的刻板印象，如 Beijing 读 [beʒɪŋ]、coup de grâce 读 [ku də ɡrɑ]。"},{"en":"Regular sound changes apply uniformly in a consistent environment, but may spread through the lexicon by lexical diffusion.","zh":"规则音变在一致的环境中统一作用，但可能通过词汇扩散逐词蔓延。"},{"en":"Sound changes may merge, split, or merely shift phonemes; the Great Vowel Shift is a chain shift without merger.","zh":"音变可导致音位合并、分裂或单纯转移；大元音移位是没有合并的链移。"}],"terms":[{"en":"metathesis","zh":"换位","defEn":"A sporadic change in which parts of the pronunciation swap positions.","defZh":"一种零星变化，发音的组成部分互换位置。"},{"en":"spelling pronunciation","zh":"拼写读音","defEn":"A change in which a word's pronunciation shifts to match its spelling.","defZh":"词的发音向拼写靠拢而变化。"},{"en":"hyperforeignism","zh":"过度外来化","defEn":"Using stereotypes about a foreign language instead of the original pronunciation.","defZh":"以外语的刻板印象取代词的原本读音。"},{"en":"lexical diffusion","zh":"词汇扩散","defEn":"The spread of a regular sound change through the lexicon word by word.","defZh":"规则音变在词库中逐词传播的过程。"},{"en":"phonemic merger","zh":"音位合并","defEn":"A regular sound change that decreases the number of phonemes in a language.","defZh":"使语言音位数量减少的规则音变。"},{"en":"chain shift","zh":"链移","defEn":"Overlapping non-merging shifts in which a newer form is another change's older form.","defZh":"多项音变重叠且不合并，一项的新形式正是另一项的旧形式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"In Old English, we find it first attested as ascian with [sk], but we soon find evidence of a metathesized form axian or acsian with [ks].","noteEn":"Metathesis in ask; the dominant [ks] variant resisted the [sk] > [ʃ] change.","noteZh":"ask 的换位：占优势的 [ks] 变体躲过了 [sk] > [ʃ] 音变。"},{"text":"[sw] > [s] / ▁ back vowel","noteEn":"A conditioned regular change, written with the environment after the slash.","noteZh":"有条件规则音变的记法，斜线后标明发生的环境。"},{"text":"cnif ‘knife’ was pronounced [kniːf], while its plural cnifas was pronounced [kniːvas]","noteEn":"[f] and [v] were allophones until French loans made them contrast.","noteZh":"在法语借词造成对立之前，[f] 与 [v] 只是同一音位的变体。"},{"text":"brycɡ > bridge and cyssen > kiss","noteEn":"An unconditioned [y] > [i] change that merged two older phonemes.","noteZh":"无条件的 [y] > [i] 音变，使两个较早的音位合并。"}],"body":[{"en":"Not all phonological change is systematic. Sporadic changes touch only a handful of words. Metathesis swaps sound positions: Old English ascian with [sk] developed a variant axian or acsian with [ks], so ask escaped the change [sk] > [ʃ] that turned fisc into fish. Similar variants appear in the ASL signs DEAF1 and DEAF2. Dissimilation, analogy, and immediate model, as when February is pronounced by model with January, are other sporadic types.","zh":"并非所有音系变化都是系统性的，零星变化只影响少数词。换位使语音位置互换：古英语 ascian 的 [sk] 发展出 axian 或 acsian 的 [ks] 变体，axian 一度占优势，使 ask 躲过了把 fisc 变成 fish 的 [sk] > [ʃ] 音变。美国手语 DEAF1 与 DEAF2 亦有类似变体。异化、类比以及即时模仿（如 February 与 January 连用而变读）都是零星变化的类型。"},{"en":"Spelling pronunciation pulls a word toward its written form: Arctic, borrowed from Middle French artique, gained [k] after being respelled from Latin arcticus, and falcon, hectic, and perfect acquired [l], [h], and [k] the same way. Hyperforeignism instead applies stereotypes about a foreign language, so Beijing is often said [beʒɪŋ] rather than [bed͡ʒɪŋ], lingerie ends in [e] rather than French [i], and coup de grâce loses its final [s].","zh":"拼写读音使发音向书写形式靠拢：Arctic 借自中古法语 artique，后来依拉丁语 arcticus 重新拼写而获得 [k]，falcon、hectic、perfect 也分别因新拼写而读出了 [l]、[h]、[k]。过度外来化则把对外语的刻板印象套在借词上：Beijing 常被读作 [beʒɪŋ] 而非 [bed͡ʒɪŋ]，lingerie 的词尾由法语的 [i] 变成 [e]，coup de grâce 的末尾 [s] 被删除。"},{"en":"Regular sound changes, by contrast, apply uniformly in a consistent environment. The Neogrammarians claimed in the late 1800s that all sound changes were regular, a proposal called the regularity principle. We now know that sporadic changes are common, and that regular changes may spread through the lexicon by lexical diffusion, reaching frequent words first; in Philadelphia, bad, glad, and mad show a raised [æ̝] before /d/, while dad and sad do not.","zh":"规则音变则像共时音系规则一样，在一致的环境中统一作用。19 世纪晚期的青年语法学派主张一切音变都是规则的，这被称为规则性原则。如今我们知道零星音变很常见，规则音变也会通过词汇扩散逐词蔓延，通常先影响高频词；在费城，bad、glad、mad 因 /d/ 前的 /æ/ 音变而读作较高的 [æ̝]，dad 和 sad 则尚未受影响。"},{"en":"Regular changes may be conditioned or unconditioned, and they can alter the phoneme inventory. A merger reduces the number of phonemes, as when /y/ merged with /i/ in brycɡ > bridge; a split increases them, as when borrowed French words gave English /v/ in contrast with /f/, as in fine and vine. A shift changes pronunciation only. The Great Vowel Shift was a chain shift of overlapping non-merging changes that raised the long vowels until [iː] and [uː] became [ai] and [au], leaving traces in pairs like divine–divinity.","zh":"规则音变可有条件，也可无条件，并会改变音位数量。合并减少音位，如 /y/ 与 /i/ 合并而有 brycɡ > bridge；分裂增加音位，如法语借词使英语的 /v/ 与 /f/ 在 fine 和 vine 中形成对立。转移只改变读音而不改音位数量。大元音移位是多项重叠而不合并的链移，长元音依次高化，[iː] 和 [uː] 最终变为 [ai] 和 [au]，并在 divine–divinity 等词对中留下痕迹。"}]},"chapter-154-slug-14-4-morphological-change":{"title":{"en":"14.4 Morphological change","zh":"14.4 形态变化"},"summary":{"en":"Morphological change reshapes inflectional paradigms and the internal structure of words. Paradigms may become more consistent through analogy, which can level allomorphy or extend a pattern taken from other verbs, and inflectional affixes can be replaced in the same way. Reanalysis shifts boundaries between morphemes, while folk etymology, eggcorns, mondegreens, and back formation reinterpret words and may create new morphemes.","zh":"形态变化既重塑屈折词形变化表，也改变词的内部结构。类比可使变化表更一致，既可能通过类推拉平减少词根语素变体，也可能依其他词的格局扩展出更多变体，屈折词缀同样会被替换。重新分析使语素边界移动，民间词源、蛋壳词、错听词与逆构词则重新解释词的构造，并可能创造新的语素。"},"points":[{"en":"Analogical levelling reduces the number of root allomorphs, as when Middle English help, halp, holp became Modern English help.","zh":"类推拉平减少词根语素变体，如中古英语的 help、halp、holp 变为现代英语的单一形式 help。"},{"en":"Analogical extension can increase allomorphs, as when Old English hring gained the ring, rang, rung pattern of sing.","zh":"类推扩展可增加语素变体，如古英语 hring 依 begin、sing 的格局变成 ring、rang、rung。"},{"en":"Reanalysis shifts a morpheme boundary, turning a napron into an apron and an ewte into a newte.","zh":"重新分析使语素边界移动，a napron 变成 an apron，an ewte 变成 a newte。"},{"en":"Folk etymology reinterprets a word's structure, as when Algonquian ochek was reinterpreted as woodchuck.","zh":"民间词源重新解释词的构造，如阿尔冈昆语的 ochek 被重新理解为 woodchuck。"},{"en":"Back formation creates new morphemes from false structure, such as emote from emotion and -holic from alcoholic.","zh":"逆构词从错误的结构中造出新语素，如由 emotion 造出 emote，由 alcoholic 造出 -holic。"}],"terms":[{"en":"paradigm","zh":"词形变化表","defEn":"The set of inflected words formed from a single root.","defZh":"由同一词根构成的一整套屈折词形。"},{"en":"syncretism","zh":"同形合并","defEn":"When two or more distinct parts of a paradigm are pronounced identically.","defZh":"词形变化表中两个或多个不同部分读音完全相同。"},{"en":"analogical levelling","zh":"类推拉平","defEn":"Analogy that reduces the number of allomorphs a root has in its paradigm.","defZh":"减少词根在变化表中语素变体数量的类比。"},{"en":"reanalysis","zh":"重新分析","defEn":"A change in which a morphological boundary shifts across one or more phones.","defZh":"形态边界越过一个或多个音素而移动的变化。"},{"en":"folk etymology","zh":"民间词源","defEn":"Treating a word as having an etymology that it does not actually have.","defZh":"把词当作具有其实际并不存在的词源。"},{"en":"back formation","zh":"逆构词","defEn":"Creating a new morpheme from a false morphological structure.","defZh":"依据错误的形态结构创造新语素。"}],"examples":[{"text":"by analogy with the rest of the swear paradigm, the [sw] was retained in all of swear’s forms, blocking the sound change from applying to swore and sworn","noteEn":"Paradigm consistency blocked a regular change in two past forms.","noteZh":"为保持变化表一致，规则的音变被阻止作用于两个过去形式。"},{"text":"a napron was reanalyzed as an apron","noteEn":"The [n] moved from the noun to the indefinite article.","noteZh":"[n] 由名词转移到不定冠词，名词随之变为 apron。"},{"text":"Old English angnægl ‘hangnail’ was originally a compound of ange ‘tight; painful’ and nægl ‘nail’","noteEn":"Folk etymology rebuilt the compound under the influence of hang.","noteZh":"民间词源在 hang 的影响下重新解释了这一复合词。"},{"text":"Some verbs like babysit and edit were back-formed from nouns (babysitter and editor)","noteEn":"New verbs were extracted from nouns that looked like verb plus -er.","noteZh":"看似动词加 -er 的名词被拆解，从中造出新的动词。"}],"body":[{"en":"Root morphemes combine with inflectional affixes to form an inflectional paradigm. The basic English verb paradigm uses ROOT, ROOT-s, ROOT-ed, and ROOT-ing, and it shows syncretism in the past tense and past participle, which share the suffix -ed. Other verbs differ: show has showed for the past but shown for the participle, while ring and go show internal change and suppletion, as in ring, rang, rung and go, went, gone.","zh":"词根语素与屈折词缀组合成屈折词形变化表。英语基本动词变化表包括 ROOT、ROOT-s、ROOT-ed 和 ROOT-ing，其中过去时与过去分词同形，都带后缀 -ed，属于同形合并。其他动词的格局不同：show 的过去时是 showed，过去分词是 shown；ring 与 go 则有内部变化和异根替换，如 ring、rang、rung 和 go、went、gone。"},{"en":"Because paradigms differ, they are a source of change; languages often make them more consistent by copying patterns from elsewhere, a process called analogy. Analogy blocked the Old English change [sw] > [s] in the past forms of swear, keeping swore and sworn consistent with swear. Analogy usually reduces the number of root allomorphs, a type called analogical levelling: Middle English help, halp, holp became help, helped, helped, like float and hope. More rarely, analogical extension increases allomorphs, as when hring became ring, rang, rung after sing.","zh":"变化表各不相同，因而成为语言变化的来源；语言常模仿别处的格局使变化表更一致，这就是类比。类比使 [sw] > [s] 音变未作用于 swear 的过去形式，swore 和 sworn 因而与 swear 保持一致。类比通常减少词根语素变体，称为类推拉平：中古英语的 help、halp、holp 变成 help、helped、helped，与 float、hope 一致。较少见的是类推扩展，如 hring 依 sing 变成 ring、rang、rung。"},{"en":"Morphological structure itself can change. In reanalysis, or rebracketing, a boundary shifts across phones while the same morphemes remain. Middle English napron was often used after the indefinite article, so a napron was reanalyzed as an apron and the noun became apron; the reverse happened when an ewte became a newte. Related words that did not undergo the change preserve the older shape, as in napkin and eft.","zh":"词的形态结构本身也会变化。重新分析（重新括弧）中，语素边界越过音素移动，而语素本身不变。中古英语 napron 常接在不定冠词后，于是 a napron 被重新分析为 an apron，名词单用即变成 apron；反向移动则使 an ewte 变成 a newte。未经历该变化的同源词保留较早形式，如 napkin 和 eft。"},{"en":"Folk etymology imposes a new structure on a word, as when Algonquian ochek was reinterpreted as the compound woodchuck. Individual misperceptions of this kind are eggcorns, such as for all intensive purposes for for all intents and purposes; when the meaning changes too, the result is a mondegreen. Back formation goes further, creating a new morpheme from a false structure: emotion yielded emote, and alcoholic yielded the productive suffix -holic in chocoholic and workaholic.","zh":"民间词源把原本没有的结构强加给词，如阿尔冈昆语 ochek 被重新理解为复合词 woodchuck。个人的这类误解称为蛋壳词，如把 for all intents and purposes 说成 for all intensive purposes；若意义也改变，则为错听词。逆构词更进一步，从错误结构造出新语素：emotion 产出 emote，alcoholic 产出能产的 -holic，如 chocoholic、workaholic。"}]},"chapter-155-slug-14-5-syntactic-change":{"title":{"en":"14.5 Syntactic change","zh":"14.5 句法变化"},"summary":{"en":"Syntactic change can convert a morphosyntactic pattern from analytic to synthetic or back again, as English negation contracted into the suffix -n't and infinitives lost their -an ending. Grammaticalization turns lexical words into functional ones, as when still became an aspectual adverb. Basic word order may also shift, as Old English SOV gave way to rigid SVO, and such changes reflect constituency and movement.","zh":"句法变化可使某种形态句法格局在分析型与综合型之间转换：英语否定词缩合成后缀 -n't，不定式则失去 -an 后缀而改用 to。语法化让词汇词变为功能词，如 still 成为体副词。基本语序也会变化，古英语的 SOV 让位于严格的 SVO，这类变化与句法成分和移位原则密切相关。"},"points":[{"en":"A pattern changes from analytic to synthetic when separate words reduce and become bound, as in have not > haven't.","zh":"独立的词弱化并附着成词缀时，格局由分析型转为综合型，如 have not > haven't。"},{"en":"The reverse change occurs when affixes erode, as when Old English infinitive -an gave way to the analytic to play.","zh":"词缀磨损则引发反向变化，如古英语不定式后缀 -an 让位于分析型的 to play。"},{"en":"Grammaticalization shifts a word from a lexical category to an abstract grammatical function, as still became an aspectual adverb.","zh":"语法化使词从词汇词类转向抽象的语法功能，如 still 成为体副词。"},{"en":"Basic word order can shift over time, as Old English SOV after pronouns gave way to rigid SVO in Modern English.","zh":"基本语序会随时间变化，古英语代词宾语时的 SOV 在现代英语中让位于严格的 SVO。"},{"en":"Word-order changes follow principles of constituency and movement, such as V-to-T movement in Middle English.","zh":"语序变化遵循句法成分与移位原则，如中古英语的 V 到 T 移位。"}],"terms":[{"en":"analytic","zh":"分析型","defEn":"Expressing a grammatical function as a free morpheme separate from the root.","defZh":"用独立于词根的自由语素表达语法功能。"},{"en":"synthetic","zh":"综合型","defEn":"Expressing a grammatical function as a bound morpheme in the same word as the root.","defZh":"用与词根同词的黏着语素表达语法功能。"},{"en":"grammaticalization","zh":"语法化","defEn":"A change in which a word shifts to a more abstract grammatical function and category.","defZh":"词转向更抽象的语法功能并改变词类的变化。"},{"en":"subject-aux inversion","zh":"主语与助动词倒装","defEn":"The movement that forms yes-no questions by inverting subject and auxiliary.","defZh":"通过主语与助动词换位构成一般疑问句的移位。"},{"en":"V-to-T movement","zh":"V 到 T 移位","defEn":"Movement of a verb from V to the tense head, as in Middle English.","defZh":"动词从 V 位置移到时制中心语，如中古英语。"}],"examples":[{"text":"They have not left.","noteEn":"The negative not is still a separate word in this alternation.","noteZh":"在这一交替中 not 仍是独立的词，与缩合形式相对。"},{"text":"Haven’t they left?","noteEn":"-n't inverts with the auxiliary, showing it is a suffix rather than a word.","noteZh":"-n't 随助动词一起倒装，说明它已是后缀而非独立的词。"},{"text":"he loued neuer sire Trystram after that","noteEn":"Middle English allowed the verb to move past the adverb neuer.","noteZh":"中古英语允许动词移到副词 neuer 之前。"},{"text":"I like chicken, but fish, I hate","noteEn":"An emphatic OSV clause, a possible seed of later word-order change.","noteZh":"强调性的 OSV 小句，可能是日后语序变化的开端。"}],"body":[{"en":"Grammatical functions may be expressed synthetically, with a bound morpheme in the same word as the root, or analytically, with a separate free morpheme. The English past tense is synthetic, while the will future is analytic. Malagasy marks past and future with bound prefixes, so both are synthetic, whereas Māori uses separate tense words before the verb, making both analytic. These labels normally describe a single pattern rather than a whole language.","zh":"语法功能既可用综合型方式表达，即用与词根同词的黏着语素，也可用分析型方式，即用独立的自由语素。英语过去时是综合型，will 将来时是分析型。马达加斯加语的过去时和将来时都用前缀，属综合型；毛利语则在动词前使用独立的时态词，两者都是分析型。这些术语通常描述的是某一具体格局，而非整门语言。"},{"en":"Patterns can shift between the two types. Separate words may reduce phonologically and collapse into one word, as when not becomes the suffix -n't: -n't must invert with the auxiliary in questions, unlike the separate word not. Conversely, affixes may erode and be replaced by separate words. Old English infinitives carried -an, as in plegian, but Middle English lost these suffixes and the analytic two-word infinitive with tō, now to play, became the only option.","zh":"格局可在两类之间转换。独立的词会发生音系弱化并合并为一个词，如 not 变成后缀 -n't：在疑问句中 -n't 必须随助动词倒装，而独立的 not 不必。反过来，词缀也可能磨损并被独立的词取代。古英语不定式带后缀 -an，如 plegian，中古英语中这些后缀消失，带 tō 的两词分析型不定式（今 to play）成为唯一形式。"},{"en":"Grammaticalization shifts a word from a lexical category to a more abstract grammatical function, usually with a change in meaning. Old English stille ‘quiet, calm, motionless’ became the aspectual adverb still, as in it is still raining, though the adjective survives in stand still. Similar shifts include willan ‘to want, wish’ > will, hwīl ‘period of time’ > while, and French chez from Latin casa ‘cottage, hut’.","zh":"语法化使词从词汇词类转向更抽象的语法功能，通常伴随意义变化。古英语形容词 stille（安静、静止）语法化为体副词 still，如 it is still raining，形容词用法仍见于 stand still。类似变化包括 willan（想要、希望）> will，hwīl（一段时间）> while，以及拉丁语 casa（小屋）> 法语 chez。"},{"en":"Basic word order can also change. Old English commonly used SVO, but SOV appeared when the object was a pronoun, as in He hit hæfde ‘He had it’. By the end of Middle English the order had become rigidly SVO, and Modern English SOV is normally ungrammatical, though emphatic OSV survives in fish, I hate. Such changes are not random: Middle English allowed V-to-T movement for main verbs, letting loued precede neuer, but Modern English does not.","zh":"基本语序也会变化。古英语常用 SVO，但宾语为代词时常用 SOV，如 He hit hæfde（他把它有了）。到中古英语末期，语序基本固定为 SVO，现代英语的 SOV 通常不合语法，只有强调性的 OSV 还见于 fish, I hate。这类变化并非随意：中古英语允许主动词的 V 到 T 移位，使 loued 出现在 neuer 之前，现代英语则不允许。"}]},"chapter-156-slug-14-6-semantic-change":{"title":{"en":"14.6 Semantic change","zh":"14.6 语义变化"},"summary":{"en":"Word meanings change over time through semantic shift, often via an intermediate polysemous stage in which old and new meanings coexist. Shifts may involve scope (widening and narrowing), association (metonymy and synecdoche), similarity (metaphor), quality (elevation and degeneration), or intensity (hyperbole and litotes). Unlike sound change, semantic change is usually sporadic and affects one word at a time, though the Chamorro directional terms shifted together as a set.","zh":"词义会随时间发生变化，通常称为语义演变或语义漂移，一般要经过新旧义并存的中间阶段，此时该词具有多义性。演变的类型包括范围变化（扩大与缩小）、关联变化（转喻与提喻）、相似性变化（隐喻）、褒贬变化（升格与降格）以及强度变化（夸张与曲言）。与音变不同，语义演变通常是零散的，一次只影响一个词，但查莫罗语方向词却作为整套系统一起发生了转变。"},"points":[{"en":"Semantic shifts usually pass through a polysemous stage where old and new meanings coexist before the older one becomes obsolete.","zh":"语义演变通常经过多义阶段，新旧义并存，随后旧义可能废弃，只留下新义。"},{"en":"Scope shifts move between a specific and a general meaning, as when arriving at shore widens to any destination.","zh":"范围变化在具体义与概括义之间移动，如 arrive 从『上岸』扩大为到达任何目的地。"},{"en":"Metonymy relies on direct association, while metaphor relies on similarity in form or function without ordinary association.","zh":"转喻依赖两个意义之间的直接关联，隐喻则依赖形式或功能上的相似，而非日常关联。"},{"en":"Quality shifts raise or lower a meaning's value, yielding elevation and degeneration and driving euphemism cycles.","zh":"褒贬变化使词义升值或贬值，形成升格与降格，并推动委婉语循环。"},{"en":"Intensity shifts weaken meaning through hyperbole or strengthen it through litotes, sometimes bleaching words into intensifiers.","zh":"强度变化通过夸张削弱词义、通过曲言增强词义，有时还把词漂白为程度词。"},{"en":"Semantic change is generally sporadic, though Chamorro directional terms rotated as a set after European contact.","zh":"语义演变一般是零散的，但查莫罗语方向词在欧洲接触后作为整套发生了旋转式变化。"}],"terms":[{"en":"semantic shift","zh":"语义演变","defEn":"Change in the meaning of a word over time, also called semantic drift.","defZh":"词的意义随时间发生的变化，又称语义漂移，通常经历新旧义并存的多义阶段。"},{"en":"widening","zh":"扩大（泛化）","defEn":"Shift from a specific meaning to a broader category that includes the original concept.","defZh":"词义从较具体的概念扩展到包含原义在内的更大范围，又称泛化、扩展或扩大。"},{"en":"narrowing","zh":"缩小（专门化）","defEn":"Shift from a general meaning to a more specific one, also called specialization or restriction.","defZh":"词义从较宽泛的概念收缩到更具体的范围，又称专门化或限制，如 deer 的演变。"},{"en":"metonymy","zh":"转喻","defEn":"Shift based on a direct association between two meanings, such as the Crown for monarchy.","defZh":"基于两个意义之间的直接关联而发生的变化，如用 Crown 指君主及其政府。"},{"en":"metaphor","zh":"隐喻","defEn":"Shift based on similarity in form or function between concepts without ordinary association.","defZh":"基于概念之间在形式或功能上的相似而发生的变化，双方通常没有日常直接关联。"},{"en":"semantic bleaching","zh":"语义漂白","defEn":"Erosion of a word's lexical content, which in the extreme leads to grammaticalization.","defZh":"词项词汇内容的磨蚀，极端情形会导致语法化，如 very 变为纯粹的程度词。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Old English bylden 'construct a house' > Modern English build 'construct anything'","noteEn":"An English example of widening, from constructing a house to constructing anything at all.","noteZh":"英语词义扩大的例子，从建造房屋扩展到建造任何事物。"},{"text":"Old English mete 'food' > Modern English meat 'animal flesh used as food'","noteEn":"Narrowing gradually restricted a general word for food to animal flesh.","noteZh":"词义缩小把泛指食物的词逐渐限制为供食用的动物肉。"},{"text":"Old English fǣr 'danger' > Modern English fear 'terror, anxiety'","noteEn":"Metonymy connects danger with the terror that people feel in its presence.","noteZh":"转喻把危险与人们面对危险时感到的恐惧直接联系起来。"},{"text":"Latin serra 'saw (tool)' > Spanish sierra 'mountain range'","noteEn":"A metaphor based on the visual similarity between saw teeth and mountain peaks.","noteZh":"隐喻来自锯齿与山峰在视觉上的相似，属形式相似。"}],"body":[{"en":"Semantic change, also called semantic drift, normally passes through a stage of polysemy in which a word carries both its older and newer meanings; eventually the older meaning may vanish. One common dimension is scope. Widening generalizes a meaning: Early Middle English ariven, once limited to reaching land after a sea voyage, became arrive, usable for any destination or means of travel. Narrowing does the reverse, as when Old English dēor, covering many animals, came to denote only the Cervidae family in Modern English deer.","zh":"语义变化又称语义漂移，通常先经过一个多义阶段，此时一个词同时承载旧义与新义，后来旧义可能消失。范围是常见的变化维度之一。词义扩大使意义泛化：早期中古英语 ariven 原指远航后靠岸登陆，演变为现代英语 arrive 后，可用于任何目的地与任何交通方式。词义缩小则相反：古英语 dēor 原可指多种动物，到现代英语 deer 时仅指鹿科动物，德语 Tier、荷兰语 dier 仍保留『动物』这一旧义。"},{"en":"Other shifts leave the original meaning's range entirely. Metonymy exploits a direct association, as when a monarch and the government are called the Crown because of the crown worn on ceremonial occasions. Synecdoche is a subtype involving a whole and its inherent part, as when glasses first named a substance, then drinking vessels and spectacles made from it (pars pro toto), or when Canada stands for its government or national teams (totum pro parte). Metaphor instead links concepts that have no ordinary association, as when grasp 'hold physically' extends to 'understand'.","zh":"另一些变化则完全跳出原有意义的范围。转喻利用两个意义之间的直接关联，例如君主及其政府因加冕场合所戴的王冠而被称为 Crown。提喻是转喻的一种，涉及整体与其固有部分：glasses 先指玻璃这种材料，后指玻璃制成的饮具与眼镜，属『部分代整体』；而 Canada 可指加拿大政府或国家队，属『整体代部分』。隐喻连接的则是彼此没有日常关联的概念，如 grasp 由『用手握住』引申为『理解』。"},{"en":"Quality shifts change how positive a meaning is. Elevation makes a meaning more favourable, as with eager, derived from Middle English egre 'angry, acidic'. Degeneration makes it less favourable, as with knave, once simply 'young man or boy' and now 'dishonest person'. Stigmatized concepts may be renamed repeatedly: euphemisms such as bathroom and restroom for toilet undergo degeneration and are replaced by new ones, forming a euphemism cycle or treadmill.","zh":"褒贬变化改变词义的褒贬倾向。升格使意义更为积极，如 eager 源自中古英语 egre『愤怒的、酸涩的』。降格使意义转向消极，如 knave 原仅指『年轻男子或男孩』，如今指『不诚实的人』。被污名化的概念往往被反复改名：bathroom、restroom 等 toilet 的委婉语一旦沾染贬义便被新说法取代，形成委婉语循环（又称委婉语跑步机）。"},{"en":"Intensity may also shift. Hyperbole weakens a meaning, as when Old English bana 'murderer' became bane 'source of harm'; carried far enough it produces semantic bleaching, turning verray 'true' into the intensifier very. Litotes strengthens a meaning, as when gruccen 'complain' became grudge. Unlike sound change, semantic change is usually sporadic, affecting single words; the Chamorro directional terms are unusual because they rotated as a whole set after European contact.","zh":"强度同样会变化。夸张使词义减弱，古英语 bana『杀人者』变为 bane『祸根』即是一例；夸张走得足够远便产生语义漂白，把 verray『真实的』变成程度词 very。曲言则使词义增强，如 gruccen『抱怨』变为 grudge『长期怨恨』。与音变不同，语义变化通常零散发生，只影响个别词；查莫罗语方向词之所以特殊，在于它们与欧洲人接触后作为整套系统一起发生了旋转式变化。"}]},"chapter-157-slug-14-8-reconstructing-the-past":{"title":{"en":"14.8 Reconstructing the past","zh":"14.8 重构过去"},"summary":{"en":"Historical linguists rely on direct written evidence for attested changes, but writing is recent and most languages have no records at all. The comparative method compares related languages and reconstructs a plausible hypothetical ancestral form, working mainly with cognates descended from a single etymon. The search is complicated by borrowings, wanderwords, false cognates, and false friends, each of which must be handled carefully.","zh":"历史语言学家依靠书面记录来研究有据可查的变化，但文字产生较晚，且大多数语言根本没有历史文献。比较法通过比较有亲缘关系的语言来构拟合理的假想祖形，其核心研究对象是源自同一祖形的同源词。寻找同源词时会遇到借词、游走词、假同源词与假朋友等干扰，这些情况都必须谨慎处理。"},"points":[{"en":"Direct written evidence reaches back only about five thousand years and omits most Indigenous and signed languages.","zh":"书面直接证据仅覆盖约五千年，且遗漏了大多数原住民语言与手语。"},{"en":"The comparative method extrapolates backwards from related languages to a single plausible hypothetical ancestral form.","zh":"比较法从有亲缘关系的语言向前回溯，构拟出一个合理的假想祖形。"},{"en":"Cognates are words or morphemes descended from the same etymon, recognized by similar sound and meaning.","zh":"同源词是源自同一祖形的词或语素，通常靠语音与意义的相似来辨认。"},{"en":"Borrowings, wanderwords, false cognates, and false friends can all mislead the comparative method.","zh":"借词、游走词、假同源词和假朋友都可能误导比较法的分析。"},{"en":"False friends are genuine cognates whose meanings diverged, so they should still be included in the comparison.","zh":"假朋友其实是真正的同源词，只是意义发生分化，因此仍应纳入比较。"}],"terms":[{"en":"comparative method","zh":"比较法","defEn":"A method comparing related languages to reconstruct a plausible hypothetical ancestral form.","defZh":"通过比较多种有亲缘关系的语言或变体，向前回溯出它们共同祖形的语言学方法。"},{"en":"cognate","zh":"同源词","defEn":"A word or morpheme in related languages descended from the same ancestor form.","defZh":"有亲缘关系的语言中直接源自同一祖形的词或语素，通常语音与意义相似。"},{"en":"etymon","zh":"祖形","defEn":"The single ancestor form from which cognates in related languages are descended.","defZh":"同源词所共同源自的那个单一祖先形式，如英语 house 与德语 Haus 的祖形。"},{"en":"borrowing","zh":"借词","defEn":"A word taken from another language, normally excluded from the comparative method.","defZh":"从另一种语言借入的词，因未经历接受语的完整历史而通常被排除在比较法之外。"},{"en":"false cognate","zh":"假同源词","defEn":"A word resembling another in sound and meaning but with a completely different history.","defZh":"语音和意义相似、看似同源，但历史来源完全不同、并非同源的词。"},{"en":"false friend","zh":"假朋友","defEn":"A true cognate whose meaning has diverged enough to obscure the relationship.","defZh":"确实是同源词，但意义已分化很大，以致不易被认出同源关系，如 gift 与 Gift。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the English word [haʊs] house and the German word [haʊs] Haus 'house' are cognates","noteEn":"Identical pronunciation and meaning make these two words obvious cognates of one etymon.","noteZh":"发音与意义几乎完全一致，使这两个词成为同一祖形的明显同源词。"},{"text":"the English word [t͡ʃɔr] chore 'task' and the German word [keːʁə] Kehre 'U-turn' are cognates","noteEn":"Their cognate relationship is obscured because both form and meaning changed greatly.","noteZh":"由于形式和意义都变化很大，它们的同源关系几乎被完全掩盖。"},{"text":"English [mr̩dr̩] murder 'kill' and German [maʁtɐ] Marter 'torture'","noteEn":"They look similar in sound and meaning but have entirely different etymologies.","noteZh":"它们语音与意义相似，但词源完全不同，属于必须排除的假同源词。"},{"text":"the English word [ɡɪft] gift and the German word [ɡɪft] Gift are pronounced essentially the same, but the German Gift means 'poison'","noteEn":"These are true cognates whose meanings diverged through elevation and degeneration.","noteZh":"它们是真同源词，意义经由升格与降格而分化，仍应纳入比较。"}],"body":[{"en":"Some language changes are attested because we have direct evidence of how they unfolded. Recordings exist only since the late 1800s, but writing reaches back to roughly 3400 BC in Sumer, giving over five thousand years of records for some languages. Thousands of languages remain unwritten, especially Indigenous languages, signed languages, and stigmatized dialects. Even documented languages are imperfectly represented, since spelling need not match pronunciation and forms like gonna are far more common in speech than in writing.","zh":"有些语言变化是有据可查的，因为我们掌握其发展过程的直接证据。录音与录像技术到十九世纪末才出现，而文字在苏美尔可追溯到约公元前 3400 年，为部分语言提供了五千多年的记录。然而成千上万种语言至今没有文字，原住民语言、手语和受污名化的方言尤其如此。即便有文献的语言也并非完美转写：拼写未必对应发音，gonna 这类形式在口语中远比书面语常见。"},{"en":"The comparative method compares related languages and extrapolates backwards to a single plausible hypothetical ancestral form, called comparative reconstruction. It applies only to languages descended from a common ancestor through ordinary language change, or genetically related. Its main objects are cognates: words or morphemes directly descended from the same ancestor form, their etymon. Because English house [haʊs] and German Haus [haʊs] match in sound and meaning, we guess that their etymon was similar, refining it to something like [huːs] given the Great Vowel Shift.","zh":"比较法把有亲缘关系的语言相互比较，向前回溯出一个合理的假想祖形，这一过程称为比较构拟。它只适用于通过常规语言变化从共同祖语分化而来的语言，即所谓有亲缘关系或发生学关系的语言。比较法的主要研究对象是同源词，即直接源自同一祖形（祖形称 etymon）的词或语素。英语 house [haʊs] 与德语 Haus [haʊs] 在语音和意义上都吻合，因此可以推测其祖形也相似，考虑到元音大推移，可进一步拟为 [huːs]。"},{"en":"Cognate hunting is full of traps. Form and meaning both drift, so English chore [t͡ʃɔr] and German Kehre [keːʁə] 'U-turn' are cognates whose relationship is nearly invisible. Borrowings resemble cognates but do not reflect the recipient language's full history, and they can make languages look more closely related than they are; the Arabic word for giraffe entered English and German separately by way of Italian. Words such as ginger, sugar, and tea, called Wanderwörter, have crossed many languages for centuries.","zh":"寻找同源词陷阱重重。形式和意义都会漂移，英语 chore [t͡ʃɔr] 与德语 Kehre [keːʁə]『掉头』虽为同源词，其关系却几乎无法辨认。借词看似同源词，却不反映接受语的全部历史，会让语言显得比实际更亲近；阿拉伯语中表示长颈鹿的词就经由意大利语分别进入英语和德语。ginger、sugar、tea 这类被称为游走词（Wanderwort）的词，数百年来穿行于多种语言之间。"},{"en":"False cognates look alike yet have unrelated histories, such as English murder and German Marter 'torture'. False friends, by contrast, are genuine cognates whose meanings diverged: English gift and German Gift look identical, but Gift means 'poison', both senses split from a neutral 'act of giving'. Because they are real cognates, false friends belong in the comparison, despite their divergent semantics. Avoiding these pitfalls yields the true cognate sets that reveal a common ancestor.","zh":"假同源词表面上相似，历史却互不相干，如英语 murder 与德语 Marter『折磨』。假朋友则相反，它们是真正的同源词，只是意义分化：英语 gift 与德语 Gift 拼写相同，但 Gift 意为『毒药』，两种意义都由中性的『给予行为』分化而来。由于假朋友确实同源，仍应纳入比较，尽管其语义已不对应。避开这些陷阱，才能得到揭示共同祖先的真正同源词集。"}]},"chapter-158-slug-14-9-case-study-reconstructing-proto-chinese":{"title":{"en":"14.9 Case study: Reconstructing Proto-Chinese","zh":"14.9 案例研究：构拟原始汉语"},"summary":{"en":"Using cognate sets from three Chinese varieties, Changsha (Xiang), Nanchang (Gan), and Suzhou (Wu), the comparative method reconstructs Proto-Chinese forms, marked with an asterisk as hypotheses. Where all three cognates match, the proto-word is identical; where they differ, correspondence sets such as p : pʰ : b reveal three distinct proto-sounds. Suzhou often looks conservative, but Nanchang preserves vowels that Changsha and Suzhou changed, so no variety is wholly conservative.","zh":"本节以长沙（湘语）、南昌（赣语）和苏州（吴语）三种汉语变体的同源词集为例，用比较法构拟原始汉语形式，并用星号标明这些形式只是假说。三者完全一致时可直接拟出相同形式；出现差异时，p : pʰ : b 这类对应集提示需要构拟三个不同的原始音。苏州常显得保守，但南昌保留了长沙和苏州已经改变的元音，因此没有哪种变体是完全保守的。"},"points":[{"en":"The data come from three Chinese varieties, Changsha (Xiang), Nanchang (Gan), and Suzhou (Wu), with tone ignored.","zh":"数据取自长沙（湘语）、南昌（赣语）和苏州（吴语）三种汉语变体，分析中不计声调。"},{"en":"An asterisk marks reconstructed forms as hypotheses, a notation originally used for diachronic reconstruction.","zh":"星号表示构拟形式只是假说，这一记号原本就用于历时构拟，后来才被借去标记不合语法。"},{"en":"Proto-words and proto-languages are abstractions that were never actually spoken by any human beings.","zh":"原始词与原始语都是抽象构拟，从未被任何人实际使用过。"},{"en":"When cognates differ, recurring correspondence sets justify positing distinct proto-sounds rather than sporadic change.","zh":"同源词出现差异时，反复出现的对应集支持设立不同的原始音，而非归因于零散变化。"},{"en":"Devoicing explains *[b] > [p] in Changsha, while the aspiration in Nanchang remains unexplained but regular.","zh":"清化可解释长沙的 *[b] > [p]，南昌的送气则尚无简单解释，但仍视为规律变化。"}],"terms":[{"en":"proto-language","zh":"原始语","defEn":"A reconstructed ancestral language, a theoretical abstraction never spoken by actual human beings.","defZh":"通过构拟得出的祖语，是理论抽象，从未被任何真实的人当作语言使用过。"},{"en":"proto-word","zh":"原始词","defEn":"A reconstructed word, the best guess at what an actual etymon was.","defZh":"构拟出的词，是对实际祖形的最佳猜测，通常用星号标示其假说性质。"},{"en":"proto-sound","zh":"原始音","defEn":"An individual reconstructed phone within a proto-word, such as *[b].","defZh":"原始词中单个构拟出的音素，如对应于 p : pʰ : b 的 *[b]。"},{"en":"correspondence set","zh":"对应集","defEn":"A set of corresponding phones across cognates, notated with colons, such as p : pʰ : b.","defZh":"同源词之间相互对应的音素集合，用冒号标记，如 p : pʰ : b 和 i : i : i。"},{"en":"devoicing","zh":"清化","defEn":"A sound change in which a voiced sound becomes voiceless, as *[b] > [p].","defZh":"浊音变为清音的音变，如长沙话中发生的 *[b] > [p]，在语言中十分常见。"},{"en":"conservative","zh":"保守","defEn":"Describing a language or variety that has changed relatively little over time.","defZh":"指在相同时期内变化较少的语言或变体，与发生了变化的创新变体相对。"}],"examples":[{"text":"比 'compare': Changsha pi, Nanchang pi, Suzhou pi, Proto-Chinese *pi","noteEn":"All three cognates match, so the proto-word is reconstructed with the same form.","noteZh":"三个同源词完全一致，因此直接拟出形式相同的原始词。"},{"text":"皮 'skin': Changsha pi, Nanchang pʰi, Suzhou bi, Proto-Chinese *bi","noteEn":"The divergent consonants form a p : pʰ : b correspondence set requiring *[b].","noteZh":"辅音各不相同，构成 p : pʰ : b 对应集，因此需要构拟 *[b]。"},{"text":"盆 'tub': Changsha pən, Nanchang pʰən, Suzhou bən, Proto-Chinese *bən","noteEn":"A second example of the same correspondence set supports regular reconstruction.","noteZh":"同一对应集的又一例证，支持把它视为规律变化而非零散变化。"},{"text":"崩 'collapse': Changsha pən, Nanchang pɛn, Suzhou pən, Proto-Chinese *pɛn","noteEn":"The vowel correspondence forces a change *[ɛ] > [ə] in Changsha and Suzhou.","noteZh":"元音的对应关系迫使人们假设长沙和苏州发生了 *[ɛ] > [ə] 的变化。"}],"body":[{"en":"The demonstration uses 2,722 cognate sets from a large dialect dictionary, but draws on just three varieties: the Changsha dialect of Xiang, the Nanchang dialect of Gan, and the Suzhou dialect of Wu. Tone is set aside because its behaviour across Chinese is too complex here. When all three cognates are pronounced identically, as with 比 'compare' [pi], [pi], [pi], the natural hypothesis is that the etymon was also [pi].","zh":"本节的演示材料取自一部收录 2722 组同源词的大型方言字汇，但只考察三种变体：湘语的长沙方言、赣语的南昌方言和吴语的苏州方言。由于声调在各汉语语言中的表现十分复杂，这里不予转写和分析。当三个同源词读音完全相同时，例如 比『compare』三地都读 [pi]，最自然的假说就是其祖形同样读 [pi]。"},{"en":"Reconstructed forms carry an asterisk, so *[pi] is a hypothesis rather than an attested fact; this notation began in diachronic linguistics and was later borrowed for ungrammaticality. Reconstructed items take the prefix proto-, giving proto-words, proto-sounds, and proto-languages, so the three varieties reconstruct Proto-Chinese. A proto-language is not a real language but a theoretical representation of a proposed historical relationship, and it was never spoken by anyone.","zh":"构拟形式前加星号，因此 *[pi] 只是假说而非有据可查的事实；这一记号原用于历时语言学，后来才被借去标记不合语法。构拟对象一律加前缀 proto-，于是有原始词、原始音和原始语，三种变体构拟出的就是原始汉语。原始语并非真实存在的语言，而是对假想历史关系的理论表述，从未有人实际使用过。"},{"en":"Divergent sets require more care. The cognates for 皮 'skin' are [pi], [pʰi], and [bi], so the word cannot be reconstructed directly; instead we isolate correspondence sets, here p : pʰ : b for the consonant and i : i : i for the vowel, and reconstruct *[i] for the vowel. Because p : p : p, pʰ : pʰ : pʰ, and p : pʰ : b each recur in many sets, they reflect regular patterns rather than sporadic change, so a third proto-sound *[b] is needed. Changsha *[b] > [p] is devoicing; Nanchang *[b] > [pʰ] has no easy explanation.","zh":"同源词不一致时需要更谨慎。皮『skin』的三个同源词为 [pi]、[pʰi]、[bi]，无法直接拟出整词；这时先切分出对应集，如辅音的 p : pʰ : b 和元音的 i : i : i，并为元音构拟 *[i]。由于 p : p : p、pʰ : pʰ : pʰ 和 p : pʰ : b 都在大量同源词集中反复出现，它们反映的是规律性模式而非零散变化，因此必须另设第三个原始音 *[b]。长沙的 *[b] > [p] 属清化；南昌的 *[b] > [pʰ] 则没有简单的解释。"},{"en":"Suzhou retains the Proto-Chinese pronunciation in most examples, suggesting it is conservative while Changsha and Nanchang are innovative. Yet 崩 'collapse' has [pən], [pɛn], [pən], which forces the reconstruction *[pɛn] alongside *[pən] for 'root', and therefore a change *[ɛ] > [ə] in Changsha and Suzhou. Every variety has changed in some respect, so languages are conservative or innovative only in particular aspects, not as wholes.","zh":"苏州在多数例子中都保留了原始汉语的读音，显得保守，而长沙和南昌较为创新。但 崩『collapse』在长沙读 [pən]、南昌读 [pɛn]、苏州读 [pən]，这就迫使我们在为『根』构拟 *[pən] 之外再为它构拟 *[pɛn]，并假设长沙和苏州发生了 *[ɛ] > [ə] 的变化。既然每种变体都在某方面发生了变化，那么所谓保守与创新只能针对语言的某些方面，而非整体。"}]},"part-016-appendix-1-alternative-to-6-14-6-21":{"title":{"en":"Appendix 1: PSRs and Flat Tree Structures","zh":"附录 1：短语结构规则与平坦树形结构"},"summary":{"en":"This appendix is offered as an alternative to the second half of the syntax chapter, Sections 6.14 to 6.21. It teaches flat tree structures instead of X-bar theory, and it is written to follow Section 6.13. It is recommended for one-semester introductory courses, and for any introductory course that has two weeks or fewer to cover syntax.","zh":"本附录是句法章节后半部分（第 6.14 至 6.21 节）的替代方案，用平坦树形结构代替 X 杠理论进行教学，内容承接第 6.13 节。它适合一学期的入门课程使用，也推荐给只有两周或更少时间讲授句法的入门课程，供教师根据课时安排灵活选择。"},"points":[{"en":"This appendix replaces the second half of the syntax chapter, that is, Sections 6.14 to 6.21.","zh":"本附录作为替代方案，取代句法章节的后半部分，也就是第 6.14 节至第 6.21 节。"},{"en":"It teaches flat tree structures instead of the X-bar structures used in the main chapter.","zh":"它讲授的是平坦树形结构，而不是正文句法章节所使用的 X 杠结构。"},{"en":"The material is written to follow directly from Section 6.13 of the syntax chapter.","zh":"本材料的内容直接承接句法章节第 6.13 节，便于学生在学完后接着学习。"},{"en":"It is recommended for one-semester introductory courses and for courses with two weeks or fewer for syntax.","zh":"推荐用于一学期的入门课程，以及只有两周或更少时间讲授句法的入门课程。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phrase structure rule (PSR)","zh":"短语结构规则","defEn":"A rule stating which elements a given kind of constituent must and may contain.","defZh":"规定某一类句法成分必须包含以及可以包含哪些元素的规则。"},{"en":"flat tree structure","zh":"平坦树形结构","defEn":"A tree diagram whose phrases are not organized into intermediate X-bar levels.","defZh":"不把短语组织成中间 X 杠层级的树形图，各成分直接附于短语节点之下。"},{"en":"X-bar theory","zh":"X 杠理论","defEn":"A theory of phrase structure that posits intermediate bar levels between words and phrases.","defZh":"一种短语结构理论，主张在词与短语之间存在中间的杠层级结构。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"This appendix is provided as an alternative to the second half of the syntax chapter, covering Sections 6.14 to 6.21. Instead of X-bar theory, it teaches flat tree structures, in which phrases are not organized into intermediate bar levels. The material is written to follow Section 6.13, so it builds directly on the phrase structure rules developed there.","zh":"本附录作为句法章节后半部分（第 6.14 至 6.21 节）的替代方案。它讲授的不是 X 杠理论，而是平坦树形结构，即不把短语组织成中间杠层级的结构。材料承接第 6.13 节，因此直接建立在那一节所建立的短语结构规则之上。"},{"en":"It is recommended to use this alternative for one-semester introductory courses, as well as any introductory courses that have two weeks or fewer to cover syntax.","zh":"对于一学期的入门课程，以及只有两周或更少时间讲授句法的入门课程，都建议采用这一替代方案。"}]},"chapter-159-a1-1-drawing-phrase-structure-rule-trees":{"title":{"en":"A1.1 Phrase Structure Rules","zh":"A1.1 短语结构规则"},"summary":{"en":"Phrase structure rules (PSRs) are the rules used to build tree diagrams and to record which phrases may occur inside or modify other phrases. They are formal hypotheses about constituency, indicating what each constituent must and may optionally contain. This section presents the textbook's final PSR list, the general template, the new CP rule for embedded clauses, and the contrasting structures of similar-looking phrases.","zh":"短语结构规则是构建树形图、记录哪些短语可以出现在其他短语内部或修饰其他短语的规则。它们是关于句法成分构成的形式化假设，说明每类成分必须包含什么、可以任选包含什么。本节给出全书最终采用的短语结构规则列表、通用模板、引入嵌入小句的新 CP 规则，以及表面相似短语在结构上的差异。"},"points":[{"en":"Phrase structure rules describe which kinds of phrases can occur inside and modify which other kinds of phrases.","zh":"短语结构规则描述哪些类型的短语可以出现在其他类型的短语内部并修饰它们。"},{"en":"In the template, elements without parentheses are obligatory and elements inside them are optional.","zh":"在通用模板中，不带括号的元素是必需的，括号内的元素则是可选的。"},{"en":"A plus sign shows that a constituent may be repeated as many times as the data requires.","zh":"加号表示这类成分可以根据需要重复出现，数量不限，可以不止一个。"},{"en":"The new CP rule introduces embedded clauses, and C stands for complementizer, including words like that, for, if and whether.","zh":"本附录新增的 CP 规则用来引入嵌入小句，其中 C 代表标句词，包括 that、for、if、whether 等词。"},{"en":"An embedded clause must always contain both a CP layer and an S layer, even when the complementizer is silent.","zh":"嵌入小句无论标句词是否在语音上出现，都必须同时具有 CP 层和 S 层。"},{"en":"Similar-looking phrases may have different structures, so a tree diagram must reflect what the sentence actually means.","zh":"表面相似的短语可能具有不同结构，因此画树形图时必须考虑句子的实际意义。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phrase structure rule (PSR)","zh":"短语结构规则","defEn":"A formal rule stating what each kind of constituent must and may contain.","defZh":"说明每一类句法成分必须包含以及可以包含哪些元素的形式化规则。"},{"en":"constituent","zh":"句法成分","defEn":"A word or group of words that functions as a unit within a larger structure.","defZh":"在更大结构中作为一个单位起作用的词或词组，即句法成分。"},{"en":"complementizer (Comp)","zh":"标句词（complementizer）","defEn":"A word such as that, for, if or whether that introduces an embedded clause.","defZh":"用来引导嵌入小句的一类功能词，例如英语中的 that、for、if、whether 等，本书记作 C 或 Comp。"},{"en":"embedded clause","zh":"嵌入小句","defEn":"A clause that appears inside another clause, most often in object position.","defZh":"出现在另一个小句内部的小句，最常见的句法位置是宾语位置。"},{"en":"Complementizer Phrase (CP)","zh":"标句词短语","defEn":"The phrase layer headed by a complementizer that contains an embedded clause.","defZh":"以标句词为中心语并包含嵌入小句的短语层级，在本书的规则中写作 CP。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I know [that syntax is fun].","noteEn":"An embedded clause in object position, introduced by the complementizer that.","noteZh":"这是位于宾语位置的嵌入小句，由标句词 that 引导而成。"},{"text":"I know [syntax is fun].","noteEn":"The complementizer is silent here, but the clause still needs a CP layer and an S layer.","noteZh":"这里的标句词是隐性的，但该小句仍然需要 CP 层和 S 层。"},{"text":"the big yellow balloon","noteEn":"Both big and yellow modify balloon, so they are two separate adjective phrases.","noteZh":"big 和 yellow 都修饰 balloon，因此它们是两个各自独立的形容词短语。"},{"text":"the very yellow balloon","noteEn":"Here very modifies yellow, so the adverb phrase is inside the adjective phrase.","noteZh":"这里的 very 修饰 yellow，因此副词短语位于形容词短语内部。"}],"body":[{"en":"Phrase structure rules, or PSRs, are the rules we use to build tree diagrams. They describe and record which kinds of phrases can occur inside and modify which other kinds of phrases. Because they are hypotheses, a sentence that does not fit them is not a disaster: we double-check our analysis first, and revise the hypothesis if the analysis was right. The final PSR list in this textbook resembles the rules from Section 6.13, with a few small additions.","zh":"短语结构规则（PSR）是我们用来构建树形图的规则。它们描述并记录哪些类型的短语可以出现在其他类型的短语内部，以及可以修饰哪些短语。由于这些规则是假设，遇到不符合规则的句子不必慌张：先检查我们是否把句子分析对了；如果分析无误，就修订假设。本书最终采用的短语结构规则列表与第 6.13 节建立的规则十分相似，只增加了少数内容。"},{"en":"PSRs take a general template form: the constituent's name appears before the arrow, and its elements are listed after the arrow from left to right. X, Y and Z are variables standing for any category. Elements without parentheses are obligatory, elements in parentheses are optional, and a plus sign allows repetition.","zh":"短语结构规则采用一种通用模板形式：箭头之前是成分的名称，箭头之后按从左到右的顺序列出该成分内部的元素。其中 X、Y、Z 是变量，可以代表名词、动词、形容词、介词、限定词等任何类别。不带括号的元素是必需的，括号内的元素是可选的，加号则表示该成分可以按需重复任意多次。"},{"en":"The CP rule is completely new here: C, or Comp, stands for complementizer and includes words like that, for, if and whether. Embedded clauses most commonly appear in object position, replacing the NP object inside the VP or the second object of a ditransitive. That is why the VP rule lists NP/CP in the second object position: the second object can be an NP or a CP, but not both. A subject embedded clause is inserted by the S rule, which also lists NP/CP.","zh":"CP 规则是本附录中全新的内容：C（即 Comp）代表标句词，包括 that、for、if、whether 等词。嵌入小句可以出现在多个位置，但最常见的是宾语位置，用来替代 VP 内的 NP 宾语，或者替代双及物结构中的第二个宾语。这正是 VP 规则在第二个宾语位置列出 NP/CP 的原因：第二个宾语可以是 NP 或 CP，但不能同时是两者。嵌入小句也可以出现在主语位置，S 规则通过在该位置列出 NP/CP 来允许这一点。"},{"en":"A common mistake when drawing embedded clauses is to miss a layer, because the complementizer can be silent in English. An embedded clause must always have both a CP layer and an S layer.","zh":"画嵌入小句时一个常见的错误是漏掉一个层级，因为英语中的标句词可以是隐性的。我们的规则不允许把 S 直接放入 VP，因此嵌入小句必须同时具有 CP 层和 S 层。"},{"en":"Two phrases may look very similar yet have different structures, so a tree diagram cannot be drawn robotically. In the big yellow balloon, big and yellow are separate adjective phrases, both attached to the NP. In the very yellow balloon, very modifies yellow, so the adverb phrase sits inside the adjective phrase, which modifies the noun.","zh":"两个短语可能看起来非常相似，结构却大不相同，因此不能机械地画树形图，而必须考虑句子的意义。在 the big yellow balloon 中，big 并不描述 yellow，所以 big 和 yellow 是两个各自独立的形容词短语，都直接附接到 NP 上。而在 the very yellow balloon 中，very 描述的是 yellow，因此副词短语修饰形容词，整个形容词短语再修饰名词。"}]},"chapter-160-a1-2-phrase-structure-rules-in-other-languages":{"title":{"en":"A1.2 Phrase Structure Rules in Other Languages","zh":"A1.2 其他语言的短语结构规则"},"summary":{"en":"Linguists often look at unfamiliar languages and describe their word order patterns with phrase structure rules. This section works through Turkish data in four steps: identifying the order of subject, object and verb, adding modifiers to constituents, looking for patterns such as optionality, and putting all the rules together. It also stresses that English translations may not share the original structure, so rules are working hypotheses to be revised.","zh":"语言学家常通过观察不熟悉的语言，用短语结构规则描述其语序规律。本节按四个步骤处理土耳其语语料：辨认主语、宾语和动词的顺序；为各成分加入修饰语；寻找可选性等规律；最后汇总全部规则。本节还强调，英语译文的结构未必与原语言相同，因此规则只是需要不断修订的工作假设。"},"points":[{"en":"The first step in writing phrase structure rules for another language is to determine constituency in the data.","zh":"为另一种语言撰写短语结构规则的第一步，是在语料中确定句法成分。"},{"en":"The VP always contains the verb and its object if there is one, but it never contains the subject.","zh":"VP 总是包含动词，如果有宾语也要把该宾语包含在内，但从不包含主语。"},{"en":"Turkish example (1) shows SOV order, and Turkish object case markers provide useful secondary evidence.","zh":"土耳其语例（1）显示 SOV 语序，土耳其语的宾语格标记则提供了有用的辅助证据。"},{"en":"English translations may not have the same structure as the original, so linguists form the simplest hypothesis and revise it with more data.","zh":"英语译文的结构未必与原语言相同，因此语言学家先提出最简单的假设，再用更多语料加以修订。"},{"en":"Because the subject can be omitted in Turkish, the S rule is written as S, with the subject NP in parentheses.","zh":"由于土耳其语中主语可以省略，S 规则写作 S → (NP) VP，也就是把主语 NP 放入括号。"},{"en":"When listing a constituent's members in a PSR, list only the elements of the next layer of structure.","zh":"在短语结构规则中列举某成分的成员时，只列出紧邻的下一层结构中的元素。"}],"terms":[{"en":"SOV word order","zh":"SOV 语序","defEn":"A default word order in which the subject precedes the object, which precedes the verb.","defZh":"一种默认语序，主语在宾语之前，宾语又在动词之前，即主语—宾语—动词。"},{"en":"case marker","zh":"格标记","defEn":"A morpheme on a noun that shows its grammatical role, such as object case.","defZh":"附在名词上、用来标示其语法角色（例如宾语格）的语素，如土耳其语的 -i。"},{"en":"structural subject","zh":"结构主语","defEn":"The NP that appears in the subject position of the clause, as the daughter of S.","defZh":"出现在小句主语位置的 NP，在树形图中充当 S 的直接成分，即结构上的主语。"},{"en":"thematic subject","zh":"题元主语","defEn":"The NP that carries the agent theta role in the sentence.","defZh":"在句子中承担施事题元角色的那个 NP，在被动句中与结构主语并不一致。"},{"en":"vowel harmony","zh":"元音和谐","defEn":"A phonological assimilation rule that makes vowels match the backness of other vowels.","defZh":"一种音系同化规则，使元音的舌位前后特征与词中其他元音一致。"},{"en":"passive","zh":"被动句","defEn":"A clause type in which the agent is not in subject position and the patient is not the object.","defZh":"一种小句类型，其中施事不在主语位置，受事也不在宾语位置。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Toprak Deniz’-i gör-dü.","noteEn":"A Turkish sentence showing SOV order, where Toprak is the subject and Deniz is the object.","noteZh":"这是一个显示 SOV 语序的土耳其语句子，其中 Toprak 是主语，Deniz 是宾语。"},{"text":"Kitap siyah masa-ya dokun-du.","noteEn":"Here siyah 'black' modifies masaya 'table', so siyah masaya forms one constituent.","noteZh":"在这个例子中，siyah（黑）修饰 masaya（桌子），因此二者构成一个句法成分。"},{"text":"Deniz’i gör-dü-m","noteEn":"The subject pronoun is absent, but the agreement marker on the verb still identifies the subject.","noteZh":"主语代词没有出现，但动词上的一致标记仍能表明主语是谁。"},{"text":"VP → (AdjP) NP V","noteEn":"An incorrect Turkish VP rule; the adjective siyah belongs inside the NP, not directly in the VP.","noteZh":"错误的土耳其语 VP 规则；形容词 siyah 属于 NP 内部，而不直接属于 VP。"}],"body":[{"en":"Linguists often examine unfamiliar languages for word order patterns and describe them with phrase structure rules. The first step is to determine constituency in the data, using the English translation to work out what modifies what. In examples from other languages, the first line is natural, the second glosses each word, and the third gives the English translation.","zh":"语言学家常常考察自己并不熟悉的语言，寻找其中的语序规律，然后用短语结构规则来描述。第一步是在语料中确定句法成分，借助英语译文的意义判断什么修饰什么。其他语言的例子通常分三行：第一行是原语言的自然写法，第二行逐词给出释义，第三行是英语译文。"},{"en":"Step 1 identifies the order of subject, object and verb. The subject is typically the NP performing the action, while the VP includes the verb and its object, never the subject. In example (1), Toprak does the seeing and Deniz is seen, so Turkish looks like an SOV language. Object case markers can help find the object, but only as secondary evidence, since their use varies.","zh":"第一步是辨认主语、宾语和动词的顺序。主语通常是执行动作的 NP，而 VP 包含动词以及动作所指向的宾语 NP；VP 从不包含主语。在土耳其语例（1）中，我们看到 Toprak 是看的人，Deniz 是被看的人，于是假设土耳其语是 SOV 语言。土耳其语还有宾语格标记，可以帮助我们找到宾语；不过并非所有语言都使用格标记，格标记的用法有时也出人意料，因此它只能作为辅助证据。"},{"en":"This approach assumes the English translation has an equivalent structure, which is not always true. In passive example (2), the one doing the seeing is not in subject position, so we distinguish the structural subject, the NP in subject position, from the thematic subject, the NP with the agent theta role. Starting from the simplest hypothesis, we gather more data and revise our rules.","zh":"这种方法假定英语译文具有与原语言相同的结构，但事实并非总是如此。在土耳其语被动句例（2）中，看的人并不在主语位置。因此有必要区分结构主语（位于主语位置的 NP）与题元主语（承担施事题元角色的 NP）；在被动句中两者并非同一个 NP。我们从最简单的假设出发，进一步收集语料，并利用动词上的被动标记、宾语上缺少格标记等线索修订规则，最终断定土耳其语确实是 SOV 语言。"},{"en":"Step 2 adds modifiers to constituents. In example (3), siyah 'black' occurs between two nouns, and the translation shows that it modifies masaya 'table', so siyah masaya forms a constituent. Turkish vowel harmony explains why the past tense marker is sometimes -dü and sometimes -du, but this does not affect the syntax. Since the subject can be omitted, the Turkish S rule places the subject NP in parentheses.","zh":"第二步为各成分加入修饰语。在例（3）中，形容词 siyah（黑）出现在两个名词之间，而英语译文告诉我们它修饰 masaya（桌子），因此 siyah masaya 构成一个句法成分。土耳其语还有元音和谐，这就是过去时标记有时是 -dü、有时是 -du 的原因，但这一差别不影响句法。由于主语可以省略，土耳其语的 S 规则把主语 NP 放入括号。"},{"en":"With a small data set, assume an element is obligatory if it appears in all relevant places. List only the next layer of structure: rules in (8) wrongly put the same AdjP inside both the VP and the NP, while the correct rules place siyah inside the NP. Step 4 collects all rules, compares them with the data, and checks them by drawing trees.","zh":"语料较少时，如果某成分在所有相关位置都出现，就应假定它是必需的，直到发现相反证据。此外，只能列出紧邻的下一层结构：例（8）中错误的规则把同一个 AdjP 同时放进 VP 和 NP，而正确的规则把 siyah 放在 NP 内部，因为它只修饰名词。第四步把所有规则汇总，与语料逐条核对，并通过画树形图来检验，最好选择最复杂的句子，因为它最有可能出错。"}]},"chapter-161-a1-2-properties-of-psr-trees":{"title":{"en":"A1.3 Properties of PSR Trees","zh":"A1.3 短语结构规则树的性质"},"summary":{"en":"Section A1.3 summarizes three properties of heads in phrase structure rules: the phrase label usually comes from the head, the head is normally the only non-phrase member of a rule, and the head is usually the obligatory part. It shows how these properties identify heads in tree diagrams, warns against two-headed structures, states the Principle of Modification, and explains how recursion in the NP and PP rules makes language infinite.","zh":"A1.3 归纳了短语结构规则中中心语的三个特点：短语标签通常取自中心语；中心语一般是规则中唯一不是短语的成员；中心语通常是唯一必须出现的成分。本节说明如何据此在树形图中辨认中心语，提醒不要画出双中心语结构，给出修饰原则，并解释 NP 与 PP 规则中的递归如何使语言具有无限性。"},"points":[{"en":"Most phrases must have a head, and the phrase label is usually named after it; S is the exception.","zh":"大多数短语都必须有中心语，短语标签通常以中心语来命名，只有 S 是例外。"},{"en":"The head is the only member of a rule that is not itself a phrase, apart from Aux, Neg, Det and Num.","zh":"中心语通常是规则中唯一不是短语的成分，但 S 规则中的 Aux、Neg 和 NP 规则中的 Det、Num 属于例外。"},{"en":"Heads are usually the only obligatory part of a phrase, though the CP rule makes its head optional.","zh":"中心语通常是短语中唯一必须出现的部分，但在 CP 规则中，中心语 Comp 反而是可以不出现的。"},{"en":"In tree diagrams the head can be identified by category matching and by the number of layers.","zh":"在树形图中，可以依据范畴是否与整个短语一致以及层次的多少来判断中心语。"},{"en":"A modifier must be the sister of the head it modifies, and a phrase never has two heads.","zh":"修饰语必须是被修饰中心语的姐妹节点，而一个短语也绝不会同时拥有两个中心语。"},{"en":"Recursion, built into the phrase structure rules, lets NPs and PPs embed inside each other and makes language infinite.","zh":"递归已经内置于短语结构规则之中，使 NP 与 PP 可以相互嵌套，语言因而具有无限性。"}],"terms":[{"en":"head","zh":"中心语","defEn":"The word in a phrase that determines the properties of the entire phrase.","defZh":"短语中决定整个短语性质的词，短语的标签通常以它命名，如 VP 中的动词。"},{"en":"phrase structure rule","zh":"短语结构规则","defEn":"A rule stating what categories a phrase may be made of and in what order.","defZh":"规定某一短语可以由哪些范畴按何种顺序组成的规则，能够生成句子的层级结构。"},{"en":"recursion","zh":"递归","defEn":"Putting something inside of itself, which allows language to be infinite.","defZh":"把某结构嵌入同类结构之中的现象，它使语言能够无限地生成新的句子。"},{"en":"Principle of Modification","zh":"修饰原则","defEn":"If an XP modifies a head Y, then XP must be Y's sister.","defZh":"若一个 XP 修饰中心语 Y，则该 XP 必须是 Y 的姐妹节点，也就是 YP 的女儿节点。"},{"en":"modifier","zh":"修饰语","defEn":"A phrase attached inside the phrase it modifies, as the sister of a head.","defZh":"位于被修饰短语内部、作为中心语姐妹节点起修饰作用的短语，如 very。"}],"examples":[{"text":"very red","noteEn":"Tree diagram example where the adjective red is the head of the phrase.","noteZh":"树形图例子：形容词 red 是整个短语的中心语，very 是它的修饰语。"},{"text":"very quickly","noteEn":"Here the adverb quickly is the head, modified by very in its own AdvP.","noteZh":"这里副词 quickly 是整个短语的中心语，very 在它自己的 AdvP 中充当修饰语。"},{"text":"the leaf on [the branch on [the tree in [the yard]]]","noteEn":"Recursive NPs and PPs, each phrase embedded inside another phrase of the same kind.","noteZh":"递归的 NP 与 PP，每一个短语都嵌入在另一个性质相同的短语之中。"},{"text":"NP → (Det) N (PP+)","noteEn":"The simplified NP rule that works with the PP rule to produce recursion.","noteZh":"简化的 NP 规则，它与 PP 规则配合使用，可以不断产生递归结构。"}],"body":[{"en":"The phrase structure rules show that most phrases must contain a head, the word that determines the properties of the whole phrase. The phrase label is usually named after that head. The only exception is S, whose label does not come from any head.","zh":"短语结构规则显示，大多数短语都必须有中心语，也就是决定整个短语性质的那个词。短语的标签通常以中心语命名，唯一的例外是 S，它的标签并不来自任何中心语。"},{"en":"Heads also stand apart from the other members of a rule in category: the head is the only element that is not itself a phrase. In the VP rule, the AdvPs, NPs, CP and PPs all end in P, while the verb does not. Aux and Neg in the S rule, and Det and Num in the NP rule, are further exceptions.","zh":"中心语的另一个特点是，它通常是规则中唯一不是短语的成员。以 VP 规则为例，其中的 AdvP、NP、CP、PP 都以 P 结尾，表示它们是短语，只有动词不是短语。S 规则中的 Aux、Neg 以及 NP 规则中的 Det、Num 也属于例外。"},{"en":"Finally, heads are usually the only obligatory element of a phrase. Exceptions include the subject and VP in the S rule and both Comp and S in the CP rule, where the head Comp is optional while the non-head S is obligatory.","zh":"中心语通常还是短语中唯一必须出现的部分。例外包括 S 规则中的主语和 VP，以及 CP 规则中的 Comp 和 S；在 CP 中，作为中心语的 Comp 是可以不出现的，而非中心语 S 反倒是必需的。"},{"en":"These properties help us find the head in a tree diagram. In very red, red is the head because its category matches that of the phrase and because very sits in an extra AdvP layer above it. In very quickly, quickly is the head, modified by very in its own AdvP; since both words are adverbs, only the number of layers reveals the head. A phrase never has two heads, and a modifier must be the sister of the head it modifies.","zh":"这些特点有助于我们在树形图中辨认中心语。在 very red 中，red 是中心语，因为它的范畴与整个短语一致，而且 very 之上还多出一个 AdvP 层次。在 very quickly 中，quickly 是中心语，very 在它自己的 AdvP 中修饰它；由于两者都是副词，只能依靠层次的多少来判断谁是中心语。一个短语绝不会有两个中心语，修饰语必须是被修饰中心语的姐妹节点。"},{"en":"Recursion is built into the phrase structure rules: because the NP rule may contain a PP and the PP rule may contain an NP, these two rules can apply over and over again, as in the leaf on [the branch on [the tree in [the yard]]]. Recursion is what allows language to be infinite, and phrase structure rules capture constituency, hierarchical structure and recursion alike.","zh":"递归已经内置于短语结构规则之中：NP 规则中可以出现 PP，PP 规则中又可以出现 NP，因此这两条规则可以反复使用，例如 the leaf on [the branch on [the tree in [the yard]]]。递归使语言具有无限性，而短语结构规则同时刻画了句法成分、层级结构和递归等语言特性。正因为语言可以递归，我们才能不断把短语嵌进同类短语之中，从而造出越来越长、数量无限的句子，这也是短语结构规则强大之处的体现。"}]},"chapter-162-a1-3-structural-ambiguity":{"title":{"en":"A1.4 Structural Ambiguity","zh":"A1.4 结构歧义"},"summary":{"en":"Section A1.4 explains structural ambiguity in syntax, where one string of words has more than one structure and each structure yields a different interpretation. Using I saw someone with a telescope, it shows a prepositional phrase modifying either the verb phrase or the noun phrase, gives paraphrases for the two readings, and applies the Principle of Modification to decide how each tree should be drawn.","zh":"A1.4 说明句法中的结构歧义：同一串词可以具有不止一种结构，每一种结构都对应不同的解释。本节以 I saw someone with a telescope 为例，说明这个介词短语既可以修饰动词短语，也可以修饰名词短语，给出两种理解各自的释义，并运用修饰原则判断应当怎样画出相应的树形图。"},"points":[{"en":"Structural ambiguity arises when one string of words has more than one structure, each with a different interpretation.","zh":"同一串词对应多种结构、而每一种结构又对应不同解释时，就产生了结构歧义。"},{"en":"I saw someone with a telescope has two readings, depending on whether the PP modifies the verb or the noun.","zh":"I saw someone with a telescope 这句话有两种理解，关键在于其中的介词短语是修饰动词还是修饰名词。"},{"en":"A paraphrase restates one meaning in new words, and paraphrases themselves should not be ambiguous.","zh":"释义就是用新的措辞表达其中一种意义，而释义本身不应当再产生新的歧义。"},{"en":"The Principle of Modification decides attachment: the PP is the sister of either the verb saw or the noun someone.","zh":"修饰原则决定附加位置：这个介词短语只能是动词 saw 或名词 someone 的姐妹节点。"}],"terms":[{"en":"structural ambiguity","zh":"结构歧义","defEn":"A situation where the same string of words has more than one possible structure.","defZh":"同一串词或语素可以对应多种结构、每种结构对应不同解释的现象。"},{"en":"paraphrase","zh":"释义","defEn":"A restatement of a sentence in new wording that keeps the same meaning.","defZh":"用不同的措辞重新表述原句、并保持意义相同的一种说法，又称改写。"},{"en":"prepositional phrase","zh":"介词短语","defEn":"A phrase headed by a preposition, often functioning as a modifier.","defZh":"以介词为中心语的短语，常充当修饰语，在句法分析中一般缩写为 PP。"},{"en":"modify","zh":"修饰","defEn":"To add information about a head by attaching a phrase to it.","defZh":"通过附加短语对中心语加以限定或补充说明的一种句法关系，又称修饰关系。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I saw someone with a telescope.","noteEn":"The ambiguous sentence whose two structures correspond to two different meanings.","noteZh":"歧义句，它的两种树形结构分别对应两种不同的意义和解释。"},{"text":"I was using a telescope, and I saw someone.","noteEn":"Paraphrase of the reading in which the PP modifies the VP.","noteZh":"介词短语修饰动词短语这一种理解所对应的释义，说明望远镜是看人的工具。"},{"text":"I saw someone, and that person had a telescope.","noteEn":"Paraphrase of the reading in which the PP modifies the NP.","noteZh":"介词短语修饰名词短语这一种理解所对应的释义，说明某人持有望远镜。"}],"body":[{"en":"In morphology we saw a first example of structural ambiguity: cases where the same string of morphemes can have more than one structure, each structure corresponding to a different interpretation. The same thing is found in syntax.","zh":"在形态学中我们已经见过结构歧义的第一个例子：同一串语素可以具有不止一种结构，而每一种结构都对应一种不同的解释。句法中也存在完全相同的现象。"},{"en":"The sentence I saw someone with a telescope has two possible interpretations. On one reading I was using a telescope and I saw someone; on the other I saw someone, and that person had a telescope.","zh":"I saw someone with a telescope 这句话有两种可能的理解：一种是我当时在使用望远镜，并且看到了某个人；另一种是我看见了一个人，而那个人带着望远镜。"},{"en":"In the first interpretation the prepositional phrase [PP with a telescope] modifies the verb phrase headed by saw. In the second interpretation the same prepositional phrase modifies the noun phrase someone. The two readings correspond to two different tree structures, and the same holds for other cases of structural ambiguity.","zh":"在第一种理解中，介词短语 [PP with a telescope] 修饰以 saw 为中心语的动词短语；在第二种理解中，同一个介词短语修饰的是名词短语 someone。这两种理解分别对应两种不同的树形结构，其他结构歧义的情况也是如此，每一种意义都会对应一种可能的树形结构。"},{"en":"When a sentence is restated with new wording, it is called a paraphrase. On an assignment you may be asked for paraphrases of the two meanings and for trees of the original sentence; make sure the paraphrases are not themselves ambiguous, and draw a tree of the original, not of the paraphrase.","zh":"用新的措辞重新表述一个句子叫做释义。在作业或考试中，可能要求你为歧义句的两种意义各写一个释义，并画出代表这两种意义的树形图；这时要注意释义本身不能再有歧义，而且必须为原句画树，而不是为你的释义画树。"},{"en":"The Principle of Modification helps us decide how to draw such sentences. If an XP modifies a head Y, then XP must be Y's sister, that is, the daughter of YP. So with a telescope can modify either the verb saw, making the PP the verb's sister, or the noun someone, making the PP the noun's sister.","zh":"修饰原则可以帮助我们决定这类歧义句的树形图应该怎么画：如果某个 XP 修饰中心语 Y，那么这个 XP 必须是 Y 的姐妹节点，也就是说必须是 YP 的女儿节点。因此 with a telescope 既可以修饰动词 saw，此时介词短语是动词的姐妹节点；也可以修饰名词 someone，此时介词短语是名词的姐妹节点。画出树形图以后，还应当为每一种结构配上恰当的释义，用来说明这个词组究竟是在修饰哪一个中心语，以及整句话因此获得了怎样的意义。"}]},"chapter-163-a1-3-head-movement-in-yes-no-questions":{"title":{"en":"A1.5 Head movement in yes-no questions","zh":"A1.5 是非问句中的中心语移位"},"summary":{"en":"Section A1.5 analyzes subject-auxiliary inversion in English yes-no questions as a case of head movement. It reviews inversion with an auxiliary and with the inserted auxiliary DO, notes that embedded questions have if or whether in the position the auxiliary occupies in main clauses, and treats inversion as moving the auxiliary from S up and to the left into C, called Aux-to-C movement, with angle-bracket notation for movement.","zh":"A1.5 把英语是非问句中的主语助动词倒装分析为一种中心语移位。本节回顾了借助原有助动词的倒装和插入助动词 DO 的倒装，指出嵌入式问句的 if 或 whether 与主句问句中助动词占据相同位置，从而把倒装看作助动词从 S 向上向左移到 C，称为助动词到 C 的移位，并介绍用尖括号标记移位的方法。"},"points":[{"en":"Yes-no questions are formed by subject-auxiliary inversion, swapping the positions of the subject and the auxiliary.","zh":"是非问句通过主语与助动词位置的交换来构成，这一操作称为主语助动词倒装。"},{"en":"If there is no auxiliary, the auxiliary word DO is inserted, and then the auxiliary DO inverts.","zh":"句中如果没有助动词，就插入助动词 DO，然后再让这个助动词 DO 发生倒装。"},{"en":"Embedded questions have the complementizer if or whether above S, in the position the auxiliary occupies in main clause questions.","zh":"嵌入式问句在 S 之上有标句词 if 或 whether，其位置与主句问句中助动词占据的位置相同。"},{"en":"Subject-auxiliary inversion can be analyzed as head movement of the auxiliary from S up and to the left into C.","zh":"主语助动词倒装可以分析为助动词从 S 向上向左移位到 C 的一种中心语移位。"},{"en":"Head movement moves a head into the next higher head position, and this instance is called Aux-to-C movement.","zh":"中心语移位把中心语移到比它高一级的中心语位置，此例称为助动词到 C 的移位。"},{"en":"In this class moved items are written in angle brackets with an arrow, and trace notation is not used.","zh":"本课程把移位的成分放进尖括号并画箭头指向落点，不使用语迹标记法。"}],"terms":[{"en":"yes-no question","zh":"是非问句","defEn":"A question that can be answered with yes or no.","defZh":"可以用「是」或「否」来回答的问句，英语中通常借助助动词移位来构成。"},{"en":"subject-auxiliary inversion","zh":"主语助动词倒装","defEn":"Swapping the positions of the subject and the auxiliary to form a question.","defZh":"构成疑问句时交换主语与助动词位置的句法操作，在英语中又称主谓倒装。"},{"en":"head movement","zh":"中心语移位","defEn":"Movement of a head (X) into the next higher head position.","defZh":"把一个中心语 X 移到比它高一级的中心语位置上的移位操作，会改变树形结构。"},{"en":"Aux-to-C movement","zh":"助动词到 C 的移位","defEn":"The head movement that moves the auxiliary in S to C.","defZh":"英语主句是非问句中把 S 里的助动词移位到 C 位置的一种中心语移位。"},{"en":"trace","zh":"语迹","defEn":"The empty position left behind by a moved element, written t.","defZh":"移位成分在原来的位置留下的空位，通常写作 t，可以看作一个变量。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Have they left?","noteEn":"Yes-no question formed from They have left by moving the auxiliary to C.","noteZh":"由 They have left 把助动词移到 C 位置所构成的是非问句，属于中心语移位。"},{"text":"Does Hari play the viola?","noteEn":"Question formed after the auxiliary DO is inserted and then inverts.","noteZh":"插入助动词 DO 之后再让它发生倒装所构成的问句，是没有助动词时的常规做法。"},{"text":"Is Iryna eating cake?","noteEn":"The auxiliary is moves in front of the subject Iryna.","noteZh":"助动词 is 移到主语 Iryna 之前所构成的问句，原来的位置留空。"},{"text":"I wonder if they have left.","noteEn":"Embedded question whose complementizer if occupies the position of the fronted auxiliary.","noteZh":"嵌入式问句，它的标句词 if 占据前移助动词在主句问句中所占据的位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Yes-no questions can be answered with yes or no and are formed by swapping the subject and the auxiliary, an operation called subject-auxiliary inversion. Examples are They have left and Have they left?, Iryna is eating cake and Is Iryna eating cake?, and The man with the long beard and the plaid shirt is waving at you and Is the man with the long beard and the plaid shirt waving at you?","zh":"是非问句是可以回答「是」或「否」的问句，其构成方式是把主语和助动词的位置互换，这一操作称为主语助动词倒装。例如 They have left 与 Have they left?，Iryna is eating cake 与 Is Iryna eating cake?，以及 The man with the long beard and the plaid shirt is waving at you 与 Is the man with the long beard and the plaid shirt waving at you?"},{"en":"If there is no auxiliary, the auxiliary word DO is inserted, and then the auxiliary DO inverts: Hari plays the viola becomes Hari does play the viola, and then Does Hari play the viola?","zh":"如果句中没有助动词，就插入助动词 DO，然后再让这个助动词 DO 倒装：Hari plays the viola 先变为 Hari does play the viola，再变为 Does Hari play the viola?"},{"en":"Inversion reverses the linear order of the subject and the auxiliary. In the tree for They have left, the structural relations encode the grammatical relations between the subject, the clause as a whole and the predicate. Those relations should not change in a question; we only change the order of constituents to mark it as a question, by moving the auxiliary up and to the left or the subject down and to the right.","zh":"倒装颠倒了主语与助动词的线性顺序。在 They have left 的树形图中，各种结构关系编码了主语、整个小句与谓语之间的语法关系。这些关系在问句中不应发生根本变化，我们只想通过改变句法成分的次序来标记疑问：或者把助动词向上向左移，或者把主语向下向右移。"},{"en":"Embedded questions have the complementizer if or whether above the S, in the same position the auxiliary occupies in main clause questions: right before the subject. Subject-auxiliary inversion can therefore be understood as movement of the auxiliary from S up and to the left, landing in C. This is Head Movement, the movement of a head into the next higher head position.","zh":"嵌入式问句在 S 之上有标句词 if 或 whether，它出现的位置与主句问句中助动词出现的位置相同，都紧挨在主语之前。因此，主语助动词倒装可以理解为助动词从 S 向上向左移位，最终落在 C 的位置。这就是中心语移位，即把中心语移到比它高一级的中心语位置。"},{"en":"Yes-no questions in English main clauses are formed by moving the auxiliary in S to C, an instance of head movement called Aux-to-C movement. This is a derivational representation: we start with one tree and change it to reach the final structure. For notation, this class puts angle brackets around the moved item and draws an arrow to its landing position; trace notation, which leaves a t behind, is not used here.","zh":"英语主句中的是非问句通过把 S 中的助动词移到 C 来构成，这种中心语移位称为助动词到 C 的移位。这是一种推导式的表示方法：先给出一个树形结构，再对它加以改动，从而得到最终的结构。至于移位的标记，本课程把移位的成分放在尖括号中，并画箭头指向它的落点；在被移位成分原来的位置留下 t 的语迹标记法，本课程不使用。除移位分析之外，语言学中还有其他方式来表示助动词与其陈述句位置之间的这种依存关系，一些非推导的句法理论正是沿着这样的思路发展的。"}]},"chapter-164-a1-4-phrasal-movement-in-wh-questions":{"title":{"en":"A1.6 Phrasal movement in wh-questions","zh":"A1.6 wh 疑问句中的短语移位"},"summary":{"en":"This section explains how content questions, or wh-questions, are built. Wh-words stand in for whole phrases and move to the front of the clause, while the auxiliary moves to C. Because the moved item is a phrase rather than a head, the operation is Phrasal Movement, or wh-movement, and the tree adds a branch to the left of C. Embedded content questions and main clause subject questions are also examined.","zh":"本节说明内容疑问句即 wh 疑问句的结构。wh 词替代的是整个短语，并移到小句之前，同时助动词移位到 C。由于移动的成分是短语而非中心语，这种操作属于短语移位，即 wh 移位，树形图在 C 左侧增加一个分支。本节还讨论了嵌入式内容疑问句和主句主语疑问句。"},"points":[{"en":"Content questions, or wh-questions, begin with a wh-word and are answered by a phrase, not by yes or no.","zh":"内容疑问句即 wh 疑问句，以 wh 词开头，回答是一个短语，而不是 yes 或 no。"},{"en":"Wh-questions show subject-auxiliary inversion, analyzed as Aux-to-C movement, just like yes-no questions.","zh":"wh 疑问句同样发生主谓倒装，可像一般疑问句那样分析为助动词移位到 C。"},{"en":"Wh-words replace whole phrases: who animate NPs, what inanimate NPs and determiners, when time, where place, why reasons, how manner, which determiners.","zh":"wh 词替换整个短语：who 有生名词短语，what 无生名词短语和限定词，when 时间，where 处所，why 原因，how 方式，which 限定词。"},{"en":"Because the auxiliary already occupies C and a whole phrase moves, this is Phrasal Movement (XP Movement), called wh-movement.","zh":"由于助动词已占据 C，而移动的是完整短语，这种操作属于短语移位（XP 移位），称为 wh 移位。"},{"en":"Embedded content questions front the wh-phrase without inversion, leaving C empty; main clause subject questions also lack inversion and do-insertion.","zh":"嵌入式内容疑问句把 wh 短语前置但不倒装，C 位置为空；主句主语疑问句也不倒装，也没有 do 插入。"}],"terms":[{"en":"wh-question","zh":"wh 疑问句","defEn":"A content question that begins with a wh-word and is answered by a phrase.","defZh":"以 wh 词开头、用短语而非 yes 或 no 回答的内容疑问句。"},{"en":"phrasal movement","zh":"短语移位","defEn":"Movement of an entire phrase into a higher phrase position.","defZh":"把一个完整的短语移入更高层的短语之中，也称 XP 移位。"},{"en":"wh-movement","zh":"wh 移位","defEn":"Movement of a wh-phrase from its original position into the CP.","defZh":"指 wh 短语从原来所在的句内位置移入 CP 的移位操作。"},{"en":"Aux-to-C movement","zh":"助动词到 C 的移位","defEn":"Movement of an auxiliary verb into the C head, producing inversion.","defZh":"助动词移入 C 中心语并造成主语与助动词倒装的移位。"},{"en":"embedded content question","zh":"嵌入式内容疑问句","defEn":"A content question inside another clause, with a fronted wh-phrase but no inversion.","defZh":"位于另一小句内部的内容疑问句，wh 短语前置但不发生倒装。"}],"examples":[{"text":"What has the squirrel hidden?","noteEn":"The wh-phrase what starts as the object of hidden and moves into the CP.","noteZh":"该 wh 短语 what 原本是 hidden 的宾语，经过 wh 移位进入 CP。"},{"text":"What kind of nuts has the squirrel hidden?","noteEn":"A complex NP moves to Spec,CP, showing that wh-movement moves phrases, not heads.","noteZh":"复杂名词短语整体移入 Spec,CP，说明 wh 移位移动的是短语而非中心语。"},{"text":"I know [CP what squirrels hide].","noteEn":"An embedded content question fronts the wh-phrase but has an empty C and no inversion.","noteZh":"嵌入式内容疑问句把 wh 短语前置，但 C 位置为空且不发生倒装。"},{"text":"Who ate the cookie? Bruno.","noteEn":"A subject question with no auxiliary and no do-insertion, so no inversion occurs.","noteZh":"主语疑问句没有助动词，也不需要 do 插入，因此不发生倒装。"}],"body":[{"en":"English content questions, or wh-questions, open with a wh-word such as who, what, which, when, where, why, or how, and they are answered by a phrase rather than by yes or no. Like yes-no questions, they show subject-auxiliary inversion, so forms such as did and is appear before the subject; this is Aux-to-C movement. The material missing from the answer is what the wh-word replaces, and wh-words substitute for whole phrases: who replaces animate NPs, what replaces inanimate NPs and determiners, when replaces time expressions, where replaces location expressions, why replaces reason CPs, how replaces manner expressions, and which replaces determiners.","zh":"英语的内容疑问句又称 wh 疑问句，句首通常是 who、what、which、when、where、why 或 how 这样的 wh 词，其回答是一个短语，而不是 yes 或 no。与一般疑问句一样，wh 疑问句也发生主谓倒装，did、is 等出现在主语之前，这可分析为助动词移位到 C，即 Aux-to-C 移位。回答中缺失的成分正是 wh 词所替换的成分，而 wh 词替换的是整个短语：who 替换有生名词短语，what 替换无生名词短语和限定词，when 替换时间表达，where 替换处所表达，why 替换表示原因的 CP，how 替换方式表达，which 替换限定词。"},{"en":"Although a wh-phrase may consist of one word, examples such as What kind of dance class and Which book about whales show that an entire phrase moves. Because the auxiliary already occupies C and the moving item is a phrase rather than a head, this cannot be head movement. It is Phrasal Movement, also called XP Movement: the wh-phrase moves from wherever it originates into the CP, an operation known as wh-movement. The tree simply adds an extra branch to the left of the C head. In What has the squirrel hidden?, what begins as the object of hidden and ends up in Spec,CP.","zh":"wh 短语有时只有一个词，但 What kind of dance class、Which book about whales 这类例子表明移动的是一个完整短语。由于助动词已经占据 C，而且移动的成分是短语而非中心语，这种移位不可能是中心语移位，而是短语移位，也称 XP 移位：wh 短语从原来的位置移入 CP，这称为 wh 移位。树形图只需在 C 中心语左侧增加一个分支。在 What has the squirrel hidden? 中，what 原本是 hidden 的宾语，最终落在 Spec,CP。"},{"en":"Embedded content questions also front the wh-phrase but skip inversion, leaving the embedded C empty; an overt complementizer such as if is impossible there. Main clause subject questions likewise show no inversion, a fact revealed by the absence of do-insertion, and linguists still disagree about why.","zh":"嵌入式内容疑问句同样把 wh 短语前置，但不发生倒装，其 C 位置为空，不能再出现 if 这样的显性标句词。主句主语疑问句也不倒装，缺少 do 插入正说明了这一点；语言学家对其原因尚无定论。"}]},"chapter-165-a1-5-draw-a-tree-step-by-step":{"title":{"en":"A1.7 Draw a Tree Step-by-Step","zh":"A1.7 一步步画树形图"},"summary":{"en":"This section gives nine steps for analyzing a sentence and drawing its tree, from identifying the main verb and subjects through classifying clauses, finding modifiers, drawing the spine, filling in phrases, marking movement, and checking the result. It stresses that analysis must come before drawing, warns about ambiguous modifiers, and explains when triangles may be used.","zh":"本节给出分析句子并绘制树形图的九个步骤，从找出主要动词和各个主语，到判断小句类型、辨认修饰语、画出骨架、填入短语、标出移位，最后复核结果。文中强调先分析后动笔，提醒注意修饰语的歧义，并说明何时可以使用三角形简写结构。"},"points":[{"en":"Step one: identify the main verb, ignoring auxiliaries; have is a main verb in I have a green spaceship but an auxiliary elsewhere.","zh":"第一步：找出主要动词，不要被助动词干扰；have 在 I have a green spaceship 中是主要动词，在其他句子里则是助动词。"},{"en":"Step two: find the subject of each verb, using question tests and agreement. Step three: identify one clause per main verb, including embedded subject and object clauses.","zh":"第二步：借助提问测试和主谓一致找出每个动词的主语。第三步：每个主要动词对应一个小句，包括作主语和作宾语的嵌入式小句。"},{"en":"Step four: classify each clause as statement, yes-no question, or content question, and locate where the wh-phrase started. Step five: identify modifiers and what they modify, watching for ambiguity.","zh":"第四步：判断每个小句是陈述句、一般疑问句还是内容疑问句，并确定 wh 短语原来的位置。第五步：找出修饰语及其修饰对象，注意歧义。"},{"en":"Step six: draw the spine, S branching to subject, auxiliary or negation, and VP, with VP branching to the V head and object; add CP above TP for questions.","zh":"第六步：画出骨架，S 下分出主语、助动词或否定词以及 VP，VP 下再分出 V 中心语和宾语；疑问句在 TP 之上加 CP。"},{"en":"Step seven: fill in subjects, objects, and modifiers, adding branches as needed; adverbs may sit left or right of the verb, PPs go right, and complex NPs are broken into pieces.","zh":"第七步：填入主语、宾语和修饰语并按需增加分支；副词可在动词左右，介词短语在右侧，复杂名词短语要逐层拆分。"},{"en":"Step eight: mark movement with angle brackets and arrows for Aux-to-C and wh-movement. Step nine: double check heads, order, crossing branches, positions, labels, and arrows.","zh":"第八步：用尖括号和箭头标出助动词到 C 的移位以及 wh 移位。第九步：复核中心语、词序、分支交叉、成分位置、词性标注和箭头。"}],"terms":[{"en":"main verb","zh":"主要动词","defEn":"The verb that heads the clause, distinct from any auxiliary verbs.","defZh":"充当小句核心、决定其论元结构的动词，与助动词相区别。"},{"en":"clause","zh":"小句","defEn":"A structure containing a subject and a predicate, one per main verb.","defZh":"包含主语和谓语的句法单位，每个主要动词对应一个小句。"},{"en":"modifier","zh":"修饰语","defEn":"An optional element such as an adjective or PP that modifies another constituent.","defZh":"形容词或介词短语等可选成分，用来修饰另一个句法成分。"},{"en":"constituent test","zh":"句法成分测试","defEn":"A diagnostic such as the movement test that shows whether words form a constituent.","defZh":"如移位测试等诊断手段，用来判断若干词是否构成一个句法成分。"},{"en":"triangle","zh":"三角形","defEn":"A shorthand that replaces branches by writing a whole constituent under a triangle.","defZh":"一种简写方式，用三角形代替分支，把整个句法成分直接写在三角形下。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I have a green spaceship.","noteEn":"Example used in Step one, where have is a main verb, not an auxiliary.","noteZh":"第一步的例子，其中 have 是主要动词而不是助动词。"},{"text":"That aliens exist surprised my sister.","noteEn":"An embedded subject clause functioning as the subject of surprised.","noteZh":"该嵌入式主语小句整体充当主要动词 surprised 的主语。"},{"text":"It is [an alien with a telescope] that you have seen.","noteEn":"The movement test shows that an alien with a telescope is a constituent.","noteZh":"移位测试表明 an alien with a telescope 是一个句法成分。"},{"text":"What have you seen?","noteEn":"Both Aux-to-C movement and wh-movement are marked with arrows in the tree.","noteZh":"树形图中用箭头同时标出助动词到 C 的移位和 wh 移位。"}],"body":[{"en":"Before drawing anything, analyze the sentence: find the main verb, locate each verb's subject, identify one clause per main verb, classify each clause, and pin down the modifiers and what they attach to. Only then draw the spine of the clause, starting from S, and fill in subjects, objects, and modifiers. Ambiguity deserves special attention: in You have seen an alien with a telescope, the PP can be sister to the noun alien, meaning that the alien owns the telescope, or sister to the verb, meaning that the telescope was used for seeing. Constituency tests such as the movement test distinguish the two structures.","zh":"动笔之前应先分析句子：找出主要动词，确定每个动词的主语，按主要动词切分小句，判断每个小句的类型，并辨认修饰语及其修饰对象。之后再从 S 开始画出小句的骨架，填入主语、宾语和修饰语。歧义尤其需要注意：在 You have seen an alien with a telescope 中，介词短语既可以与名词 alien 构成姐妹节点，表示外星人拿着望远镜，也可以与动词构成姐妹节点，表示用望远镜看。可用移位测试等句法成分测试区分这两种结构。"},{"en":"For the spine itself, S typically branches two to four ways, for the subject, any auxiliary or negation, and the VP; the VP then branches into the V head and an optional object. Embedded subject clauses go on the far-left branch under S, embedded object clauses on the right branch under VP, with their CP headed by that or a null C. Complex NPs are broken down one piece at a time, as in the outlandish lady with the purple purse from Wal-Mart on her elegant arm.","zh":"画骨架时，S 下通常有两到四个分支，分别对应主语、助动词或否定词以及 VP；VP 下再分出一到两个分支，对应 V 中心语和宾语。嵌入式主语小句放在 S 下最左侧的分支，嵌入式宾语小句放在 VP 下的右侧分支，其 CP 的 C 中心语写作 that 或为空。若名词短语较复杂，可像 The outlandish lady with the purple purse from Wal-Mart on her elegant arm 那样逐层拆分：先确定 lady 是中心语，再处理层层嵌套的介词短语。"},{"en":"Questions add a CP above the TP and require movement to be marked: angle brackets around the auxiliary left behind, a copy under C, and an arrow; for wh-movement the wh-phrase is shown in its original position in angle brackets and rewritten in the specifier of CP with its internal structure drawn. Finally, check every answer: every phrase needs a head, branches must not cross, word order must be right, subjects belong under TP, objects under VP, and modifiers must be sisters to what they modify. Triangles abbreviate structure but may cost marks.","zh":"疑问句要在 TP 之上加一个 CP，并表示出移位：用尖括号标出留在原位的助动词，在 C 下重写助动词并画箭头；发生 wh 移位时，先用尖括号在原始位置标出 wh 短语，再把它的标签写入 CP 的指示语位置，并在下方画出其内部结构。最后要复核：每个短语都要有中心语，分支不能交叉，词序要正确，主语在 TP 之下，宾语在 VP 之下，修饰语必须与所修饰成分构成姐妹节点。三角形可用来简写结构，但考试中可能得不到满分，最好只用于草稿，最后仍要补全。"}]}});
